window.READING_REVIEW_DATA = {"items":[{"id":"jeans-3eb874ba0149","term":"jeans","type":"word","sourceOrder":1,"zh":"牛仔裤，复数形式","pos":"n. pl.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a pair of jeans 一条牛仔裤 · wear trousers 穿裤子","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Thanks for coming, Tom and Sophie. So you’re doing a project on jeans with a multimedia display and a written report.","zh":"谢谢你们来，Tom 和 Sophie。你们正在做牛仔裤项目，成果包括多媒体展示和书面报告。","source":"original","number":2},{"en":"Please bring a pair of jeans for the outdoor activity.","zh":"户外活动请带一条牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I usually wear jeans rather than formal trousers.","zh":"我通常穿牛仔裤，而不是正式长裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The museum displays a pair of jeans worn by a factory worker.","zh":"博物馆展出一条工厂工人穿过的牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Durable trousers such as jeans can reduce the need for frequent replacement.","zh":"牛仔裤等耐用长裤可以减少频繁更换的需要。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-ccccb03cac07","term":"a pair of jeans","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":2,"zh":"一条牛仔裤","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"a pair of jeans 一条牛仔裤 · wear trousers 穿裤子","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And we were really lucky because they had a pair from that exact same year.","zh":"我们很幸运，因为他们正好有一条产自同一年的牛仔裤。","source":"original","number":16},{"en":"Please bring a pair of jeans for the outdoor activity.","zh":"户外活动请带一条牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I usually wear jeans rather than formal trousers.","zh":"我通常穿牛仔裤，而不是正式长裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The museum displays a pair of jeans worn by a factory worker.","zh":"博物馆展出一条工厂工人穿过的牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Durable trousers such as jeans can reduce the need for frequent replacement.","zh":"牛仔裤等耐用长裤可以减少频繁更换的需要。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-1b5f82125c8e","term":"trousers","type":"word","sourceOrder":3,"zh":"裤子，复数形式","pos":"n. pl.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a pair of jeans 一条牛仔裤 · wear trousers 穿裤子","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But it’s actually from the Italian city of Genoa, where they made a similar fabric in the sixteenth century that was used for trousers worn by sailors.","zh":"但按材料所说，这个名称实际来自意大利城市 Genoa；当地十六世纪制作一种类似布料，用来做水手穿的裤子。","source":"original","number":6},{"en":"Please bring a pair of jeans for the outdoor activity.","zh":"户外活动请带一条牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I usually wear jeans rather than formal trousers.","zh":"我通常穿牛仔裤，而不是正式长裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The museum displays a pair of jeans worn by a factory worker.","zh":"博物馆展出一条工厂工人穿过的牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Durable trousers such as jeans can reduce the need for frequent replacement.","zh":"牛仔裤等耐用长裤可以减少频繁更换的需要。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-99b94ab3f768","term":"denim","type":"word","sourceOrder":4,"zh":"牛仔布、丹宁布","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"blue denim 蓝色牛仔布 · cotton fabric 棉织物","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"In fact, before we started the project, we both assumed it was somewhere in France because that’s where the jeans fabric, the denim, was first made.","zh":"实际上，做项目前，我们都以为这个名称源于法国某处，因为制作牛仔裤的布料 denim 最早产自那里。","source":"original","number":5},{"en":"The samples include blue denim and brown cotton duck.","zh":"样品包括蓝色牛仔布和棕色棉帆布。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I prefer clothes made from soft cotton fabric.","zh":"我更喜欢柔软棉布制成的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article compares denim with other types of cloth.","zh":"文章比较牛仔布与其他布料。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Choosing durable fabrics can extend the useful life of clothing.","zh":"选择耐用布料可以延长衣服的使用寿命。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-ad2a542c84c7","term":"fabric","type":"word","sourceOrder":5,"zh":"织物、布料","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"blue denim 蓝色牛仔布 · cotton fabric 棉织物","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"In fact, before we started the project, we both assumed it was somewhere in France because that’s where the jeans fabric, the denim, was first made.","zh":"实际上，做项目前，我们都以为这个名称源于法国某处，因为制作牛仔裤的布料 denim 最早产自那里。","source":"original","number":5},{"en":"The samples include blue denim and brown cotton duck.","zh":"样品包括蓝色牛仔布和棕色棉帆布。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I prefer clothes made from soft cotton fabric.","zh":"我更喜欢柔软棉布制成的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article compares denim with other types of cloth.","zh":"文章比较牛仔布与其他布料。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Choosing durable fabrics can extend the useful life of clothing.","zh":"选择耐用布料可以延长衣服的使用寿命。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d6e28ffb3b19","term":"cloth","type":"word","sourceOrder":6,"zh":"布、布料","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"blue denim 蓝色牛仔布 · cotton fabric 棉织物","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I thought that was quite good, but I must admit, I thought some of the technical stuff about making the cloth could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"我觉得那部分不错，但必须承认，有些布料制作的技术内容原本可以表达得更清楚。","source":"original","number":35},{"en":"The samples include blue denim and brown cotton duck.","zh":"样品包括蓝色牛仔布和棕色棉帆布。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I prefer clothes made from soft cotton fabric.","zh":"我更喜欢柔软棉布制成的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article compares denim with other types of cloth.","zh":"文章比较牛仔布与其他布料。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Choosing durable fabrics can extend the useful life of clothing.","zh":"选择耐用布料可以延长衣服的使用寿命。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-b2adbc5c3322","term":"cotton duck","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":7,"zh":"棉帆布，duck 在此不是鸭子","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"duck 在这里为结实的帆布，不是鸭子。 · blue denim 蓝色牛仔布 · cotton fabric 棉织物","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"They used them on both the jeans made from blue denim and those made of something called cotton duck, which was actually brown.","zh":"他们在蓝色 denim 制成的牛仔裤，以及棕色棉帆布 cotton duck 制成的牛仔裤上，都用了这种铆钉。","source":"original","number":14},{"en":"The samples include blue denim and brown cotton duck.","zh":"样品包括蓝色牛仔布和棕色棉帆布。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I prefer clothes made from soft cotton fabric.","zh":"我更喜欢柔软棉布制成的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article compares denim with other types of cloth.","zh":"文章比较牛仔布与其他布料。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Choosing durable fabrics can extend the useful life of clothing.","zh":"选择耐用布料可以延长衣服的使用寿命。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-80974e50413f","term":"sailor","type":"word","sourceOrder":8,"zh":"水手","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"trousers worn by sailors 水手穿的裤子 · rural communities 乡村社区","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But it’s actually from the Italian city of Genoa, where they made a similar fabric in the sixteenth century that was used for trousers worn by sailors.","zh":"但按材料所说，这个名称实际来自意大利城市 Genoa；当地十六世纪制作一种类似布料，用来做水手穿的裤子。","source":"original","number":6},{"en":"This display shows the trousers worn by sailors.","zh":"这块展板展示水手穿的裤子。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I read a story about a sailor from rural America.","zh":"我读过一个来自美国乡村的水手的故事。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The exhibition describes clothing worn by sailors and rural workers.","zh":"展览介绍水手和乡村工人穿的衣物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Clothing can reveal important differences between rural and maritime communities.","zh":"服装可以揭示乡村社区与海事社区的重要差异。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-896b6c3808e8","term":"rural America","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":9,"zh":"美国乡村地区","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"trousers worn by sailors 水手穿的裤子 · rural communities 乡村社区","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But nowadays, most people associate jeans with rural America, the sorts of thing that farmers and workmen wore in the nineteenth century and afterwards.","zh":"不过如今，多数人把牛仔裤与美国乡村联系起来，也就是十九世纪及以后农民和工人穿着的那类衣物。","source":"original","number":7},{"en":"This display shows the trousers worn by sailors.","zh":"这块展板展示水手穿的裤子。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I read a story about a sailor from rural America.","zh":"我读过一个来自美国乡村的水手的故事。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The exhibition describes clothing worn by sailors and rural workers.","zh":"展览介绍水手和乡村工人穿的衣物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Clothing can reveal important differences between rural and maritime communities.","zh":"服装可以揭示乡村社区与海事社区的重要差异。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-78195eddbaf6","term":"cowboy movie","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":10,"zh":"牛仔电影、西部片","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a clip from a movie 电影片段 · a film excerpt 一段电影节选","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","source":"original","number":8},{"en":"We will show a short clip from a cowboy movie.","zh":"我们将播放一段牛仔电影短片段。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I watched a film excerpt before reading the book.","zh":"读书前我看了一段电影片段。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The short clip illustrates life in a nineteenth-century town.","zh":"短片段展示十九世纪小镇的生活。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Film excerpts can make historical topics more engaging for students.","zh":"电影片段可以让历史主题对学生更有吸引力。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-26b20f3b041f","term":"short clip","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":11,"zh":"短片段","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a clip from a movie 电影片段 · a film excerpt 一段电影节选","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","source":"original","number":8},{"en":"We will show a short clip from a cowboy movie.","zh":"我们将播放一段牛仔电影短片段。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I watched a film excerpt before reading the book.","zh":"读书前我看了一段电影片段。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The short clip illustrates life in a nineteenth-century town.","zh":"短片段展示十九世纪小镇的生活。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Film excerpts can make historical topics more engaging for students.","zh":"电影片段可以让历史主题对学生更有吸引力。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-c254b43a405c","term":"film excerpt","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":12,"zh":"电影片段","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"题面 except 应为 excerpt。except 是“除……以外”。 · a clip from a movie 电影片段 · a film excerpt 一段电影节选","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","source":"original","number":8},{"en":"We will show a short clip from a cowboy movie.","zh":"我们将播放一段牛仔电影短片段。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I watched a film excerpt before reading the book.","zh":"读书前我看了一段电影片段。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The short clip illustrates life in a nineteenth-century town.","zh":"短片段展示十九世纪小镇的生活。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Film excerpts can make historical topics more engaging for students.","zh":"电影片段可以让历史主题对学生更有吸引力。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-8740066e3fea","term":"costume designs","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":13,"zh":"戏服设计、时代服装设计","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"historically accurate costumes 符合历史的服装 · accurate for the period 符合那个年代","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","source":"original","number":9},{"en":"The costume designs are accurate for the period.","zh":"服装设计符合那个时期。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I liked the film’s detailed costume designs.","zh":"我喜欢电影细致的服装设计。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Researchers checked whether the costumes were accurate for the period.","zh":"研究者核对服装是否符合那个年代。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Accurate costume designs can help audiences understand historical settings.","zh":"准确的服装设计有助于观众理解历史背景。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-57510478941d","term":"accurate for the period","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":14,"zh":"符合那个时期","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"historically accurate costumes 符合历史的服装 · accurate for the period 符合那个年代","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","source":"original","number":9},{"en":"The costume designs are accurate for the period.","zh":"服装设计符合那个时期。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I liked the film’s detailed costume designs.","zh":"我喜欢电影细致的服装设计。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Researchers checked whether the costumes were accurate for the period.","zh":"研究者核对服装是否符合那个年代。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Accurate costume designs can help audiences understand historical settings.","zh":"准确的服装设计有助于观众理解历史背景。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-62f5d588fd39","term":"pocket","type":"word","sourceOrder":15,"zh":"口袋","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"jeans pockets 牛仔裤口袋 · a clothing manufacturer 服装制造商","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays, manufacturers use all sorts of fancy stitches and designs on jeans pockets.","zh":"如今，制造商会在牛仔裤口袋上使用各种花哨缝线和图案。","source":"original","number":12},{"en":"The manufacturer added a small pocket inside the jacket.","zh":"制造商在夹克内加了一个小口袋。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I like jeans with deep pockets.","zh":"我喜欢有深口袋的牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The manufacturer reinforced the pockets to prevent damage.","zh":"制造商加固口袋以防损坏。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Clothing manufacturers should balance attractive designs with practical features.","zh":"服装制造商应平衡美观设计与实用功能。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-10002859ace9","term":"manufacturer","type":"word","sourceOrder":16,"zh":"制造商","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"jeans pockets 牛仔裤口袋 · a clothing manufacturer 服装制造商","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"The manufacturer added a small pocket inside the jacket.","zh":"制造商在夹克内加了一个小口袋。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I like jeans with deep pockets.","zh":"我喜欢有深口袋的牛仔裤。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The manufacturer reinforced the pockets to prevent damage.","zh":"制造商加固口袋以防损坏。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Clothing manufacturers should balance attractive designs with practical features.","zh":"服装制造商应平衡美观设计与实用功能。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-e91a14485f42","term":"fancy stitches","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":17,"zh":"花式缝线","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"decorative stitching 装饰缝线 · fancy stitches on pockets 口袋上的花式缝线","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays, manufacturers use all sorts of fancy stitches and designs on jeans pockets.","zh":"如今，制造商会在牛仔裤口袋上使用各种花哨缝线和图案。","source":"original","number":12},{"en":"Notice the fancy stitches around the pockets.","zh":"请注意口袋周围的花式缝线。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I prefer simple stitching to fancy designs.","zh":"我更喜欢简洁缝线，而不是花哨设计。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The catalogue highlights the jacket’s decorative stitches.","zh":"目录突出展示夹克的装饰针脚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Fancy stitching may attract buyers without improving a garment’s durability.","zh":"花式缝线可能吸引买家，但不一定提高衣服的耐用性。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-864a42c4bf81","term":"stitch","type":"word","sourceOrder":18,"zh":"针脚、缝线，也可作动词“缝”","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"decorative stitching 装饰缝线 · fancy stitches on pockets 口袋上的花式缝线","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays, manufacturers use all sorts of fancy stitches and designs on jeans pockets.","zh":"如今，制造商会在牛仔裤口袋上使用各种花哨缝线和图案。","source":"original","number":12},{"en":"Notice the fancy stitches around the pockets.","zh":"请注意口袋周围的花式缝线。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I prefer simple stitching to fancy designs.","zh":"我更喜欢简洁缝线，而不是花哨设计。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The catalogue highlights the jacket’s decorative stitches.","zh":"目录突出展示夹克的装饰针脚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Fancy stitching may attract buyers without improving a garment’s durability.","zh":"花式缝线可能吸引买家，但不一定提高衣服的耐用性。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-a15b59a0a350","term":"copper rivets","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":19,"zh":"铜铆钉","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"attach pockets with rivets 用铆钉固定口袋 · copper rivets 铜铆钉","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"The copper rivets keep the pockets firmly attached.","zh":"铜铆钉让口袋牢固固定。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I noticed small copper rivets on my jeans.","zh":"我注意到牛仔裤上有小铜铆钉。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The designer used copper rivets to reinforce weak points.","zh":"设计师用铜铆钉加固薄弱处。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Simple features such as rivets can improve the durability of clothing.","zh":"铆钉等简单设计可以提高衣服耐用性。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d16f06fe255d","term":"copper","type":"word","sourceOrder":20,"zh":"铜","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"attach pockets with rivets 用铆钉固定口袋 · copper rivets 铜铆钉","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"The copper rivets keep the pockets firmly attached.","zh":"铜铆钉让口袋牢固固定。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I noticed small copper rivets on my jeans.","zh":"我注意到牛仔裤上有小铜铆钉。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The designer used copper rivets to reinforce weak points.","zh":"设计师用铜铆钉加固薄弱处。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Simple features such as rivets can improve the durability of clothing.","zh":"铆钉等简单设计可以提高衣服耐用性。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-992952a966f8","term":"rivet","type":"word","sourceOrder":21,"zh":"铆钉","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"attach pockets with rivets 用铆钉固定口袋 · copper rivets 铜铆钉","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"The copper rivets keep the pockets firmly attached.","zh":"铜铆钉让口袋牢固固定。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I noticed small copper rivets on my jeans.","zh":"我注意到牛仔裤上有小铜铆钉。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The designer used copper rivets to reinforce weak points.","zh":"设计师用铜铆钉加固薄弱处。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Simple features such as rivets can improve the durability of clothing.","zh":"铆钉等简单设计可以提高衣服耐用性。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-0038eda1db57","term":"utilitarian","type":"word","sourceOrder":22,"zh":"注重实用的","pos":"adj.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"utilitarian clothing 实用型服装 · the utilitarian side 实用性这一面","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"The display focuses on the utilitarian side of the design.","zh":"展览重点介绍设计的实用性。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I like clothes that are comfortable and utilitarian.","zh":"我喜欢舒适实用的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Early customers valued the utilitarian features of the trousers.","zh":"早期顾客重视裤子的实用功能。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Utilitarian design can reduce unnecessary decoration and improve function.","zh":"实用设计可以减少不必要的装饰，改善功能。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-21b1282f95fc","term":"the utilitarian side of things","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":23,"zh":"事物实用性的一面","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"utilitarian clothing 实用型服装 · the utilitarian side 实用性这一面","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"The display focuses on the utilitarian side of the design.","zh":"展览重点介绍设计的实用性。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I like clothes that are comfortable and utilitarian.","zh":"我喜欢舒适实用的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Early customers valued the utilitarian features of the trousers.","zh":"早期顾客重视裤子的实用功能。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Utilitarian design can reduce unnecessary decoration and improve function.","zh":"实用设计可以减少不必要的装饰，改善功能。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-54dab9eb6d32","term":"durable","type":"word","sourceOrder":24,"zh":"耐用的","pos":"adj.","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"durable = long-lasting，但第25题否定耐用性是如今主要关注点；应选持续流行。 · durable clothing 耐用衣物 · comfortable and tough 舒适又耐穿","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"That’s really the thing about jeans. And although they’re so durable, that’s not what people think about these days.","zh":"这才是牛仔裤的关键魅力。虽然它们很耐用，但这并不是如今人们主要考虑的事。","source":"original","number":21},{"en":"You will need comfortable, tough trousers for this activity.","zh":"这项活动需要舒适结实的裤子。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I choose durable jeans because I wear them often.","zh":"我选择耐用牛仔裤，因为经常穿。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The fabric remained comfortable and tough after repeated washing.","zh":"反复洗涤后布料仍舒适结实。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Durable and comfortable clothing can offer better value over time.","zh":"耐用舒适的衣物长期来看可能更划算。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-dede1e000407","term":"tough","type":"word","sourceOrder":25,"zh":"结实耐磨的","pos":"adj.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"durable clothing 耐用衣物 · comfortable and tough 舒适又耐穿","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But I think we need to add something about using jeans for work because they’re so comfortable and tough.","zh":"但我认为应补充牛仔裤用于工作的内容，因为它们舒适又耐穿。","source":"original","number":32},{"en":"You will need comfortable, tough trousers for this activity.","zh":"这项活动需要舒适结实的裤子。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I choose durable jeans because I wear them often.","zh":"我选择耐用牛仔裤，因为经常穿。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The fabric remained comfortable and tough after repeated washing.","zh":"反复洗涤后布料仍舒适结实。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Durable and comfortable clothing can offer better value over time.","zh":"耐用舒适的衣物长期来看可能更划算。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-46fd05f35b55","term":"comfortable","type":"word","sourceOrder":26,"zh":"舒适的","pos":"adj.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"durable clothing 耐用衣物 · comfortable and tough 舒适又耐穿","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But I think we need to add something about using jeans for work because they’re so comfortable and tough.","zh":"但我认为应补充牛仔裤用于工作的内容，因为它们舒适又耐穿。","source":"original","number":32},{"en":"You will need comfortable, tough trousers for this activity.","zh":"这项活动需要舒适结实的裤子。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I choose durable jeans because I wear them often.","zh":"我选择耐用牛仔裤，因为经常穿。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The fabric remained comfortable and tough after repeated washing.","zh":"反复洗涤后布料仍舒适结实。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Durable and comfortable clothing can offer better value over time.","zh":"耐用舒适的衣物长期来看可能更划算。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-f3ffba520f6b","term":"designer labels","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":27,"zh":"设计师品牌","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a favourite designer label 最喜爱的设计师品牌 · different brands and styles 不同品牌与款式","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And then you’ve got a section in your display about designer labels.","zh":"接着，你们的展示里有一块关于设计师品牌的内容。","source":"original","number":23},{"en":"The next section compares several designer labels.","zh":"下一部分比较几个设计师品牌。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I care more about comfort than designer labels.","zh":"比起设计师品牌，我更在意舒适。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The survey explored students’ preferences for different brands and styles.","zh":"调查探讨学生对不同品牌款式的偏好。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Designer labels can influence purchasing decisions through branding.","zh":"设计师品牌可以通过品牌塑造影响购买决策。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-5db990b7999e","term":"brands and styles","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":28,"zh":"品牌与款式","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a favourite designer label 最喜爱的设计师品牌 · different brands and styles 不同品牌与款式","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Okay, we’ll see what we can come up with. Now, the next section we called Variety. We’ve got a lot about different brands and styles of jeans.","zh":"好的，我们看看能提出些什么。下一部分叫“多样性”，已写了很多不同品牌和款式的内容。","source":"original","number":31},{"en":"The next section compares several designer labels.","zh":"下一部分比较几个设计师品牌。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I care more about comfort than designer labels.","zh":"比起设计师品牌，我更在意舒适。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The survey explored students’ preferences for different brands and styles.","zh":"调查探讨学生对不同品牌款式的偏好。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Designer labels can influence purchasing decisions through branding.","zh":"设计师品牌可以通过品牌塑造影响购买决策。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-3a245342b1c5","term":"multimedia display","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":29,"zh":"多媒体展示","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"prepare a multimedia display 准备多媒体展示 · revise a report draft 修改报告草稿","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Thanks for coming, Tom and Sophie. So you’re doing a project on jeans with a multimedia display and a written report.","zh":"谢谢你们来，Tom 和 Sophie。你们正在做牛仔裤项目，成果包括多媒体展示和书面报告。","source":"original","number":2},{"en":"Please submit the draft of your written report on Friday.","zh":"请周五提交书面报告草稿。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"We prepared a multimedia display for our class project.","zh":"我们为课堂项目准备了多媒体展示。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The written report explains the research behind the display.","zh":"书面报告解释展示背后的研究。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Combining a multimedia display with a written report can develop different skills.","zh":"结合多媒体展示与书面报告可以培养不同技能。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-5d9e97a52cc4","term":"written report","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":30,"zh":"书面报告","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"prepare a multimedia display 准备多媒体展示 · revise a report draft 修改报告草稿","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Thanks for coming, Tom and Sophie. So you’re doing a project on jeans with a multimedia display and a written report.","zh":"谢谢你们来，Tom 和 Sophie。你们正在做牛仔裤项目，成果包括多媒体展示和书面报告。","source":"original","number":2},{"en":"Please submit the draft of your written report on Friday.","zh":"请周五提交书面报告草稿。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"We prepared a multimedia display for our class project.","zh":"我们为课堂项目准备了多媒体展示。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The written report explains the research behind the display.","zh":"书面报告解释展示背后的研究。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Combining a multimedia display with a written report can develop different skills.","zh":"结合多媒体展示与书面报告可以培养不同技能。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-7743ce348d92","term":"draft","type":"word","sourceOrder":31,"zh":"草稿","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"prepare a multimedia display 准备多媒体展示 · revise a report draft 修改报告草稿","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Uh, now let’s look at possible improvements to the draft of your written report.","zh":"现在来看看书面报告草稿可以怎样改进。","source":"original","number":27},{"en":"Please submit the draft of your written report on Friday.","zh":"请周五提交书面报告草稿。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"We prepared a multimedia display for our class project.","zh":"我们为课堂项目准备了多媒体展示。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The written report explains the research behind the display.","zh":"书面报告解释展示背后的研究。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Combining a multimedia display with a written report can develop different skills.","zh":"结合多媒体展示与书面报告可以培养不同技能。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-1ca7aaa322fb","term":"lecturer","type":"word","sourceOrder":32,"zh":"大学讲师、教师","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"discuss a project with a lecturer 与讲师讨论项目 · engage an audience 吸引观众","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"You will hear two fashion students called Tom and Sophie discussing their project on jeans with their lecturer.","zh":"你将听到两位时装专业学生 Tom 和 Sophie 与他们的讲师讨论牛仔裤项目。","source":"original","number":1},{"en":"The lecturer will introduce the project to the audience.","zh":"讲师将向观众介绍项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Our lecturer encouraged us to think about our audience.","zh":"讲师鼓励我们考虑受众。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The audience asked the lecturer several questions about the exhibition.","zh":"观众就展览向讲师提了几个问题。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Lecturers can help students adapt their presentations to different audiences.","zh":"讲师可以帮助学生使展示适合不同受众。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-adf0e0999386","term":"audience","type":"word","sourceOrder":33,"zh":"观众、听众","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"discuss a project with a lecturer 与讲师讨论项目 · engage an audience 吸引观众","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","source":"original","number":9},{"en":"The lecturer will introduce the project to the audience.","zh":"讲师将向观众介绍项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Our lecturer encouraged us to think about our audience.","zh":"讲师鼓励我们考虑受众。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The audience asked the lecturer several questions about the exhibition.","zh":"观众就展览向讲师提了几个问题。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Lecturers can help students adapt their presentations to different audiences.","zh":"讲师可以帮助学生使展示适合不同受众。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-181fdd46fc4a","term":"origin","type":"word","sourceOrder":34,"zh":"起源、来源","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the origin of a word 一个词的起源 · come from a place 来自某地","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"So you’ve got a map to show where the name jeans comes from.","zh":"你们准备了一张地图，用来展示 jeans 这个名称的来源。","source":"original","number":4},{"en":"The map shows where the name comes from.","zh":"地图显示名称来自哪里。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in the origin of everyday words.","zh":"我对日常词汇的起源感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article traces the origin of the name to an Italian city.","zh":"文章把名称起源追溯到意大利一座城市。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Understanding where a product comes from can deepen consumers’ knowledge of it.","zh":"了解产品来自哪里可以加深消费者对它的认识。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-cc63c363b0a9","term":"come from","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":35,"zh":"来自、源于","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the origin of a word 一个词的起源 · come from a place 来自某地","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"So you’ve got a map to show where the name jeans comes from.","zh":"你们准备了一张地图，用来展示 jeans 这个名称的来源。","source":"original","number":4},{"en":"The map shows where the name comes from.","zh":"地图显示名称来自哪里。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in the origin of everyday words.","zh":"我对日常词汇的起源感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article traces the origin of the name to an Italian city.","zh":"文章把名称起源追溯到意大利一座城市。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Understanding where a product comes from can deepen consumers’ knowledge of it.","zh":"了解产品来自哪里可以加深消费者对它的认识。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d5d80178ac30","term":"historical context","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":36,"zh":"历史背景","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"来自题目选项。录音用服装符合时代、让观众感受 setting 来表达。 · provide historical context 提供历史背景 · the setting of a film 电影背景","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","source":"original","number":9},{"en":"The clip provides historical context for the exhibition.","zh":"短片为展览提供历史背景。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I liked the film’s rural setting.","zh":"我喜欢电影的乡村背景。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The introduction explains the historical context of the design.","zh":"引言解释设计的历史背景。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Historical context can help students interpret objects more accurately.","zh":"历史背景可以帮助学生更准确地理解物品。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-ec72b9566a9c","term":"setting","type":"word","sourceOrder":37,"zh":"背景环境、场景","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"provide historical context 提供历史背景 · the setting of a film 电影背景","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","source":"original","number":9},{"en":"The clip provides historical context for the exhibition.","zh":"短片为展览提供历史背景。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I liked the film’s rural setting.","zh":"我喜欢电影的乡村背景。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The introduction explains the historical context of the design.","zh":"引言解释设计的历史背景。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Historical context can help students interpret objects more accurately.","zh":"历史背景可以帮助学生更准确地理解物品。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-8de4cd7e1428","term":"take out a patent on","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":38,"zh":"为……取得专利","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"take out a patent on a design 取得设计专利 · a patented invention 受专利保护的发明","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And we went to the museum because we wanted to see if they had something from eighteen seventy-three, because that was the year when Levi Strauss took out a patent on his design for jeans.","zh":"我们去博物馆，想看看有没有 1873 年的藏品，因为按材料所说，那一年 Levi Strauss 为他的牛仔裤设计取得了专利。","source":"original","number":15},{"en":"The inventor took out a patent on the new design.","zh":"发明者为新设计取得了专利。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I read about someone who patented a useful tool.","zh":"我读到有人为一件实用工具申请了专利。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The company took out a patent on its manufacturing process.","zh":"公司为制造工艺取得专利。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Patents can reward innovation while limiting competitors’ use of an invention.","zh":"专利可以奖励创新，同时限制竞争者使用发明。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-4cd6b391db6a","term":"patent","type":"word","sourceOrder":39,"zh":"专利","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"take out a patent on a design 取得设计专利 · a patented invention 受专利保护的发明","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And we went to the museum because we wanted to see if they had something from eighteen seventy-three, because that was the year when Levi Strauss took out a patent on his design for jeans.","zh":"我们去博物馆，想看看有没有 1873 年的藏品，因为按材料所说，那一年 Levi Strauss 为他的牛仔裤设计取得了专利。","source":"original","number":15},{"en":"The inventor took out a patent on the new design.","zh":"发明者为新设计取得了专利。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I read about someone who patented a useful tool.","zh":"我读到有人为一件实用工具申请了专利。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The company took out a patent on its manufacturing process.","zh":"公司为制造工艺取得专利。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Patents can reward innovation while limiting competitors’ use of an invention.","zh":"专利可以奖励创新，同时限制竞争者使用发明。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-33789d4bdf8a","term":"wall hangings","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":40,"zh":"墙面悬挂展示品","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"use jeans as wall hangings 把牛仔裤用作墙面展示品 · decorative wall hangings 装饰性壁挂","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, for the wall hangings, we’ll use our own jeans and those of our friends and family. We’ve got some going back to the sixties.","zh":"墙上的展示品会使用我们自己以及亲友的牛仔裤，其中一些可以追溯到二十世纪六十年代。","source":"original","number":19},{"en":"The wall hangings will be installed tomorrow.","zh":"墙面展示品明天安装。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"We used old clothes as wall hangings for the project.","zh":"我们用旧衣物作为项目的墙面展示品。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The wall hangings represent several decades of fashion.","zh":"墙面展示品呈现了几十年的时尚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Creative wall hangings can make exhibitions more visually engaging.","zh":"有创意的墙面展示品可以增强展览的视觉吸引力。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-21c0fbc5d08a","term":"attraction","type":"word","sourceOrder":41,"zh":"吸引力、魅力","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the main attraction 主要吸引力 · a significant attraction 重要吸引力","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Now, in your display, you’re planning to have a wall with thirty pairs of jeans hung on it. The wall’s titled The Attraction of Jeans. What exactly is their most significant attraction?","zh":"你们计划在展示中设置一面挂三十条牛仔裤的墙，题为“牛仔裤的魅力”。它们最主要的吸引力究竟是什么？","source":"original","number":18},{"en":"What is the most significant attraction of this design?","zh":"这种设计最主要的吸引力是什么？","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"For me, the main attraction of jeans is comfort.","zh":"对我来说，牛仔裤的主要吸引力是舒适。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The survey identified price as the product’s main attraction.","zh":"调查发现价格是产品的主要吸引力。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"A product’s main attraction may change as consumer preferences develop.","zh":"随着消费者偏好变化，产品的主要吸引力可能改变。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-32c744299c39","term":"the most significant attraction","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":42,"zh":"最主要的吸引力","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the main attraction 主要吸引力 · a significant attraction 重要吸引力","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Now, in your display, you’re planning to have a wall with thirty pairs of jeans hung on it. The wall’s titled The Attraction of Jeans. What exactly is their most significant attraction?","zh":"你们计划在展示中设置一面挂三十条牛仔裤的墙，题为“牛仔裤的魅力”。它们最主要的吸引力究竟是什么？","source":"original","number":18},{"en":"What is the most significant attraction of this design?","zh":"这种设计最主要的吸引力是什么？","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"For me, the main attraction of jeans is comfort.","zh":"对我来说，牛仔裤的主要吸引力是舒适。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The survey identified price as the product’s main attraction.","zh":"调查发现价格是产品的主要吸引力。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"A product’s main attraction may change as consumer preferences develop.","zh":"随着消费者偏好变化，产品的主要吸引力可能改变。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-42614d9c6d9b","term":"quotes from celebrities","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":43,"zh":"名人引语","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"quotes from celebrities 名人引语 · magazine advertisements 杂志广告","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"We’d thought of looking on the Internet for quotes from celebrities about their favorite designer labels, and we found some, but they didn’t really say much, so we abandoned that.","zh":"我们也想过上网找名人谈最喜爱设计师品牌的引语，确实找到了，但内容没什么实质信息，所以放弃了。","source":"original","number":26},{"en":"Please compare the celebrity quotes with the magazine advertisements.","zh":"请比较名人引语与杂志广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I rarely buy something just because a celebrity recommends it.","zh":"我很少仅因名人推荐就购买某物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The magazine advertisements included quotes from several celebrities.","zh":"杂志广告包含几位名人的引语。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Celebrity endorsements in advertisements can influence young consumers.","zh":"广告中的名人代言可以影响年轻消费者。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d9e218ac870d","term":"celebrity","type":"word","sourceOrder":44,"zh":"名人","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"quotes from celebrities 名人引语 · magazine advertisements 杂志广告","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"We’d thought of looking on the Internet for quotes from celebrities about their favorite designer labels, and we found some, but they didn’t really say much, so we abandoned that.","zh":"我们也想过上网找名人谈最喜爱设计师品牌的引语，确实找到了，但内容没什么实质信息，所以放弃了。","source":"original","number":26},{"en":"Please compare the celebrity quotes with the magazine advertisements.","zh":"请比较名人引语与杂志广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I rarely buy something just because a celebrity recommends it.","zh":"我很少仅因名人推荐就购买某物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The magazine advertisements included quotes from several celebrities.","zh":"杂志广告包含几位名人的引语。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Celebrity endorsements in advertisements can influence young consumers.","zh":"广告中的名人代言可以影响年轻消费者。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-bda67dcb5673","term":"magazine advertisements","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":45,"zh":"杂志广告","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"quotes from celebrities 名人引语 · magazine advertisements 杂志广告","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"So then we considered cutting out ads for designer jeans from magazines, and we found some really good ones.","zh":"于是我们考虑从杂志上剪下设计师品牌牛仔裤的广告，也找到了一些很不错的。","source":"original","number":25},{"en":"Please compare the celebrity quotes with the magazine advertisements.","zh":"请比较名人引语与杂志广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I rarely buy something just because a celebrity recommends it.","zh":"我很少仅因名人推荐就购买某物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The magazine advertisements included quotes from several celebrities.","zh":"杂志广告包含几位名人的引语。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Celebrity endorsements in advertisements can influence young consumers.","zh":"广告中的名人代言可以影响年轻消费者。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-655b17c9f540","term":"relevant examples","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":46,"zh":"相关例子","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"relevant examples 相关例子 · illustrate a point 阐明一个观点","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Your section on history is very interesting, and I think you’ve illustrated your points more than adequately with relevant examples.","zh":"你们的历史部分很有趣，而且我认为你们已用相关例子相当充分地说明了观点。","source":"original","number":28},{"en":"Please illustrate your main points with relevant examples.","zh":"请用相关例子阐明主要观点。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I find ideas easier to understand when people use relevant examples.","zh":"有相关例子时，我觉得观点更容易理解。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report illustrates its points with examples from local businesses.","zh":"报告用当地企业的例子阐明观点。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Relevant examples can strengthen an argument by making it more concrete.","zh":"相关例子可以使论证更具体，从而增强说服力。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-60f1344874ed","term":"illustrate points with examples","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":47,"zh":"用例子阐明观点","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"这里 illustrate 是用例子说明观点；visual illustrations 才指图解。 · relevant examples 相关例子 · illustrate a point 阐明一个观点","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Your section on history is very interesting, and I think you’ve illustrated your points more than adequately with relevant examples.","zh":"你们的历史部分很有趣，而且我认为你们已用相关例子相当充分地说明了观点。","source":"original","number":28},{"en":"Please illustrate your main points with relevant examples.","zh":"请用相关例子阐明主要观点。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I find ideas easier to understand when people use relevant examples.","zh":"有相关例子时，我觉得观点更容易理解。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report illustrates its points with examples from local businesses.","zh":"报告用当地企业的例子阐明观点。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Relevant examples can strengthen an argument by making it more concrete.","zh":"相关例子可以使论证更具体，从而增强说服力。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-02ed252717a6","term":"practical uses","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":48,"zh":"实际用途、实用用途","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"practical uses of jeans 牛仔裤的实用用途 · have a practical use 具有实际用途","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But I think we need to add something about using jeans for work because they’re so comfortable and tough.","zh":"但我认为应补充牛仔裤用于工作的内容，因为它们舒适又耐穿。","source":"original","number":32},{"en":"Add more information about the practical uses of the material.","zh":"补充这种材料实际用途的信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I prefer gifts that have a practical use.","zh":"我更喜欢有实际用途的礼物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article lists several practical uses for recycled fabric.","zh":"文章列出再生布料的几种实用用途。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Research should consider practical uses as well as theoretical value.","zh":"研究应同时考虑实际用途和理论价值。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-66ff250b6fa5","term":"step-by-step drawings","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":49,"zh":"分步图解","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"对应 Manufacturing 章节的 visual illustrations。 · drawings to go with the text 配合文字的图解 · visual illustrations 视觉图示","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I think it would be much easier if we had some step-by-step drawings to go with the text.","zh":"我觉得如果有配合文字的分步图解，就会容易理解得多。","source":"original","number":36},{"en":"Use step-by-step drawings to explain the process.","zh":"用分步图解解释过程。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I understand instructions better with visual illustrations.","zh":"有图示时我更容易理解说明。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The manual combines step-by-step drawings with short explanations.","zh":"手册结合分步图解与简短说明。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Visual illustrations can make technical information easier to understand.","zh":"视觉图示可以让技术信息更容易理解。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-8391370ff4cc","term":"visual illustrations","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":50,"zh":"视觉图示","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"drawings to go with the text 配合文字的图解 · visual illustrations 视觉图示","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I think it would be much easier if we had some step-by-step drawings to go with the text.","zh":"我觉得如果有配合文字的分步图解，就会容易理解得多。","source":"original","number":36},{"en":"Use step-by-step drawings to explain the process.","zh":"用分步图解解释过程。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I understand instructions better with visual illustrations.","zh":"有图示时我更容易理解说明。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The manual combines step-by-step drawings with short explanations.","zh":"手册结合分步图解与简短说明。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Visual illustrations can make technical information easier to understand.","zh":"视觉图示可以让技术信息更容易理解。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-92bdb9f59628","term":"global aspects","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":51,"zh":"全球层面的内容","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a global phenomenon 全球现象 · global aspects of marketing 营销的全球层面","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And in fact, marketing jeans is a huge phenomenon covering all corners of the earth. And your report should reflect that, shouldn’t it?","zh":"实际上，牛仔裤营销是遍及全球的现象，你们的报告也应体现这一点，对吧？","source":"original","number":40},{"en":"The final section should discuss global aspects of the industry.","zh":"最后一部分应讨论行业的全球层面。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in fashion as a global phenomenon.","zh":"我对时尚作为全球现象很感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article describes online shopping as a global phenomenon.","zh":"文章把网购描述为全球现象。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Studying global aspects of consumption can reveal differences between markets.","zh":"研究消费的全球层面可以揭示市场之间的差异。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-3754c68d4b05","term":"phenomenon","type":"word","sourceOrder":52,"zh":"现象","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a global phenomenon 全球现象 · global aspects of marketing 营销的全球层面","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And in fact, marketing jeans is a huge phenomenon covering all corners of the earth. And your report should reflect that, shouldn’t it?","zh":"实际上，牛仔裤营销是遍及全球的现象，你们的报告也应体现这一点，对吧？","source":"original","number":40},{"en":"The final section should discuss global aspects of the industry.","zh":"最后一部分应讨论行业的全球层面。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in fashion as a global phenomenon.","zh":"我对时尚作为全球现象很感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article describes online shopping as a global phenomenon.","zh":"文章把网购描述为全球现象。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Studying global aspects of consumption can reveal differences between markets.","zh":"研究消费的全球层面可以揭示市场之间的差异。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d83571a00094","term":"bestseller","type":"word","sourceOrder":53,"zh":"畅销品，不限于畅销书","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"remain a bestseller 保持畅销 · become a bestseller 成为畅销品","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Will jeans still be bestsellers, say, in ten years’ time?","zh":"比如，十年后牛仔裤还会是畅销品吗？","source":"original","number":30},{"en":"The jacket has remained a bestseller for five years.","zh":"这款夹克已连续畅销五年。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"That novel became a bestseller, so I decided to read it.","zh":"那本小说成了畅销书，所以我决定读它。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The company’s original jeans remain its biggest bestseller.","zh":"公司最初的牛仔裤仍是最畅销的产品。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"A bestseller may lose popularity when consumer tastes change.","zh":"消费者品味改变时，畅销品可能不再受欢迎。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-c06ba4f2490a","term":"do a project on","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":54,"zh":"做关于……的项目","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"do a project on fashion 做时尚项目 · start with the introduction 从引言开始","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Thanks for coming, Tom and Sophie. So you’re doing a project on jeans with a multimedia display and a written report.","zh":"谢谢你们来，Tom 和 Sophie。你们正在做牛仔裤项目，成果包括多媒体展示和书面报告。","source":"original","number":2},{"en":"Let’s have a look at your project and start with the display.","zh":"看看你们的项目，先从展示开始。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m doing a project on local fashion.","zh":"我正在做当地时尚的项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The class started with a look at an earlier project on clothing.","zh":"课堂先查看此前的服装项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Projects on local issues can give students a useful starting point for research.","zh":"当地议题项目可以为学生研究提供有用起点。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-507143b56862","term":"have a look at","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":55,"zh":"查看、看一看","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"do a project on fashion 做时尚项目 · start with the introduction 从引言开始","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Thanks for coming, Tom and Sophie. So you’re doing a project on jeans with a multimedia display and a written report.","zh":"谢谢你们来，Tom 和 Sophie。你们正在做牛仔裤项目，成果包括多媒体展示和书面报告。","source":"original","number":2},{"en":"Let’s have a look at your project and start with the display.","zh":"看看你们的项目，先从展示开始。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m doing a project on local fashion.","zh":"我正在做当地时尚的项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The class started with a look at an earlier project on clothing.","zh":"课堂先查看此前的服装项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Projects on local issues can give students a useful starting point for research.","zh":"当地议题项目可以为学生研究提供有用起点。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-6f60c858b018","term":"start with","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":56,"zh":"从……开始","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"do a project on fashion 做时尚项目 · start with the introduction 从引言开始","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I’ve had a look at the plans for the display. Let’s start with that.","zh":"我看过展示方案了，我们先从这部分开始。","source":"original","number":3},{"en":"Let’s have a look at your project and start with the display.","zh":"看看你们的项目，先从展示开始。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m doing a project on local fashion.","zh":"我正在做当地时尚的项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The class started with a look at an earlier project on clothing.","zh":"课堂先查看此前的服装项目。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Projects on local issues can give students a useful starting point for research.","zh":"当地议题项目可以为学生研究提供有用起点。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-ab833eda2e84","term":"assume that","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":57,"zh":"以为、假定……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"第21题问做项目前的想法；assumed 对应 France，而 actually 对应后来的发现。 · assume that something is true 以为某事是真的 · before starting a project 开始项目前","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"In fact, before we started the project, we both assumed it was somewhere in France because that’s where the jeans fabric, the denim, was first made.","zh":"实际上，做项目前，我们都以为这个名称源于法国某处，因为制作牛仔裤的布料 denim 最早产自那里。","source":"original","number":5},{"en":"Before we started the project, we assumed the fabric was French.","zh":"开始项目前，我们以为布料是法国的。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I assumed the shop was open, but I was wrong.","zh":"我以为商店开着，结果错了。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The students questioned what they had assumed before the project.","zh":"学生质疑了项目开始前的假设。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Researchers should examine assumptions rather than assume that familiar claims are true.","zh":"研究者应检查假设，而不是认为熟悉的说法必然真实。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-39ba623fec6b","term":"before we started the project","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":58,"zh":"在开始项目前","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"assume that something is true 以为某事是真的 · before starting a project 开始项目前","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"In fact, before we started the project, we both assumed it was somewhere in France because that’s where the jeans fabric, the denim, was first made.","zh":"实际上，做项目前，我们都以为这个名称源于法国某处，因为制作牛仔裤的布料 denim 最早产自那里。","source":"original","number":5},{"en":"Before we started the project, we assumed the fabric was French.","zh":"开始项目前，我们以为布料是法国的。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I assumed the shop was open, but I was wrong.","zh":"我以为商店开着，结果错了。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The students questioned what they had assumed before the project.","zh":"学生质疑了项目开始前的假设。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Researchers should examine assumptions rather than assume that familiar claims are true.","zh":"研究者应检查假设，而不是认为熟悉的说法必然真实。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-4de41cab3ebc","term":"associate A with B","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":59,"zh":"把 A 与 B 联系起来","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"associate jeans with rural America 把牛仔裤与美国乡村联系起来 · associate price with quality 把价格与质量联系起来","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But nowadays, most people associate jeans with rural America, the sorts of thing that farmers and workmen wore in the nineteenth century and afterwards.","zh":"不过如今，多数人把牛仔裤与美国乡村联系起来，也就是十九世纪及以后农民和工人穿着的那类衣物。","source":"original","number":7},{"en":"Many people associate this brand with outdoor activities.","zh":"许多人把该品牌与户外活动联系起来。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I associate jeans with comfort.","zh":"我把牛仔裤与舒适联系起来。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Consumers often associate handmade products with quality.","zh":"消费者常把手工产品与质量联系起来。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Advertising can encourage consumers to associate a product with a particular lifestyle.","zh":"广告可以让消费者把产品与某种生活方式联系起来。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-abcb664e60ca","term":"become increasingly popular","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":60,"zh":"变得越来越流行","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"increasingly popular products 越来越受欢迎的产品 · grow in popularity 越来越流行","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","source":"original","number":8},{"en":"Online exhibitions are becoming increasingly popular.","zh":"线上展览正变得越来越流行。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Second-hand clothes have become increasingly popular among my friends.","zh":"二手衣物在我朋友中越来越受欢迎。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Cycling became increasingly popular after new routes were built.","zh":"新路线修建后，骑行越来越受欢迎。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Flexible working has become increasingly popular as technology improves.","zh":"随着技术改善，弹性工作越来越受欢迎。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-55e2ef7facdb","term":"make someone do something","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":61,"zh":"使某人做某事","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"make someone decide 让某人作出决定 · make someone think 让某人思考","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","source":"original","number":8},{"en":"What made you decide to use this film clip?","zh":"是什么让你决定使用这段电影？","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The high price made me change my mind.","zh":"高价让我改变了主意。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The exhibition made visitors think about clothing waste.","zh":"展览让游客思考服装浪费。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Well-designed lessons can make students question familiar assumptions.","zh":"精心设计的课程可以让学生质疑熟悉的假设。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-c8b76c12e709","term":"give someone a feel for","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":62,"zh":"让某人感受、了解……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"第22题说明电影片段的作用：帮助观众感受历史场景，不是直接解释流行原因。 · give the audience a feel for the setting 让观众感受背景 · get a feel for a place 感受一个地方","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","source":"original","number":9},{"en":"The clip gives the audience a feel for life at sea.","zh":"短片让观众感受海上生活。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The photos gave me a feel for the town.","zh":"照片让我对小镇有了直观感受。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The introduction gives readers a feel for the period.","zh":"引言让读者感受那个时代。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Museum displays can give students a feel for life in the past.","zh":"博物馆展示可以让学生感受过去的生活。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-9efb8d3af819","term":"all sorts of","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":63,"zh":"各种各样的","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"all sorts of designs 各种设计 · be interested in practical features 关注实用功能","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays, manufacturers use all sorts of fancy stitches and designs on jeans pockets.","zh":"如今，制造商会在牛仔裤口袋上使用各种花哨缝线和图案。","source":"original","number":12},{"en":"Visitors interested in fashion can see all sorts of designs.","zh":"对时尚感兴趣的游客可以看到各种设计。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in all sorts of art.","zh":"我对各种艺术都感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The shop sells all sorts of clothes for customers interested in outdoor activities.","zh":"商店为对户外活动感兴趣的顾客出售各种衣物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"People interested in lifelong learning should have access to different kinds of courses.","zh":"对终身学习感兴趣的人应能接触不同课程。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-f93d40b90a57","term":"be interested in","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":64,"zh":"对……感兴趣、关注……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"all sorts of designs 各种设计 · be interested in practical features 关注实用功能","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays, manufacturers use all sorts of fancy stitches and designs on jeans pockets.","zh":"如今，制造商会在牛仔裤口袋上使用各种花哨缝线和图案。","source":"original","number":12},{"en":"Visitors interested in fashion can see all sorts of designs.","zh":"对时尚感兴趣的游客可以看到各种设计。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in all sorts of art.","zh":"我对各种艺术都感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The shop sells all sorts of clothes for customers interested in outdoor activities.","zh":"商店为对户外活动感兴趣的顾客出售各种衣物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"People interested in lifelong learning should have access to different kinds of courses.","zh":"对终身学习感兴趣的人应能接触不同课程。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-3d997239a725","term":"make sure","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":65,"zh":"确保……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"make sure the pockets are secure 确保口袋牢固 · get torn off 被扯掉","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"Make sure the pocket doesn’t get torn off.","zh":"确保口袋不会被扯掉。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The button got torn off when I caught my coat on the door.","zh":"外套挂在门上时扣子被扯掉了。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The manufacturer strengthened the seams to make sure they would not tear.","zh":"制造商加固接缝以确保不会撕裂。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Product testing can help manufacturers make sure clothing withstands everyday use.","zh":"产品测试能帮助制造商确保衣物经得起日常使用。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-fe6dfae29872","term":"get torn off","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":66,"zh":"被扯掉","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"make sure the pockets are secure 确保口袋牢固 · get torn off 被扯掉","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"Make sure the pocket doesn’t get torn off.","zh":"确保口袋不会被扯掉。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The button got torn off when I caught my coat on the door.","zh":"外套挂在门上时扣子被扯掉了。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The manufacturer strengthened the seams to make sure they would not tear.","zh":"制造商加固接缝以确保不会撕裂。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Product testing can help manufacturers make sure clothing withstands everyday use.","zh":"产品测试能帮助制造商确保衣物经得起日常使用。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d7d1bc5ffa68","term":"both A and B","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":67,"zh":"A 和 B 两者都","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"both denim and cotton duck 牛仔布和棉帆布两者 · be made of cotton 由棉制成","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"They used them on both the jeans made from blue denim and those made of something called cotton duck, which was actually brown.","zh":"他们在蓝色 denim 制成的牛仔裤，以及棕色棉帆布 cotton duck 制成的牛仔裤上，都用了这种铆钉。","source":"original","number":14},{"en":"Both jackets are made of cotton.","zh":"两件夹克都是棉制的。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I like bags made from recycled materials.","zh":"我喜欢再生材料制成的包。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Both the blue and brown trousers were made from durable fabrics.","zh":"蓝色和棕色裤子都由耐用布料制成。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Products made from recycled materials can benefit both consumers and the environment.","zh":"再生材料制成的产品可以同时惠及消费者与环境。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-95cc9a8c9533","term":"be made from","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":68,"zh":"由……制成","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"both denim and cotton duck 牛仔布和棉帆布两者 · be made of cotton 由棉制成","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"They used them on both the jeans made from blue denim and those made of something called cotton duck, which was actually brown.","zh":"他们在蓝色 denim 制成的牛仔裤，以及棕色棉帆布 cotton duck 制成的牛仔裤上，都用了这种铆钉。","source":"original","number":14},{"en":"Both jackets are made of cotton.","zh":"两件夹克都是棉制的。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I like bags made from recycled materials.","zh":"我喜欢再生材料制成的包。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Both the blue and brown trousers were made from durable fabrics.","zh":"蓝色和棕色裤子都由耐用布料制成。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Products made from recycled materials can benefit both consumers and the environment.","zh":"再生材料制成的产品可以同时惠及消费者与环境。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-45e716946f6e","term":"be made of","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":69,"zh":"由……制成","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"both denim and cotton duck 牛仔布和棉帆布两者 · be made of cotton 由棉制成","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"They used them on both the jeans made from blue denim and those made of something called cotton duck, which was actually brown.","zh":"他们在蓝色 denim 制成的牛仔裤，以及棕色棉帆布 cotton duck 制成的牛仔裤上，都用了这种铆钉。","source":"original","number":14},{"en":"Both jackets are made of cotton.","zh":"两件夹克都是棉制的。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I like bags made from recycled materials.","zh":"我喜欢再生材料制成的包。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Both the blue and brown trousers were made from durable fabrics.","zh":"蓝色和棕色裤子都由耐用布料制成。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Products made from recycled materials can benefit both consumers and the environment.","zh":"再生材料制成的产品可以同时惠及消费者与环境。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-60b51ddcf7a8","term":"take something away","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":70,"zh":"把某物带走","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"take the jeans away 把牛仔裤带走 · take a photo of the display 拍下展示","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"They couldn’t let us take them away, of course, but they did let us take a photo of them.","zh":"当然，他们不能让我们把裤子带走，但确实允许我们拍照。","source":"original","number":17},{"en":"You may take a photo of the object, but you cannot take it away.","zh":"可以拍摄展品，但不能带走。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I took a photo of the jacket instead of buying it.","zh":"我拍了夹克的照片，没有买它。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Visitors were allowed to photograph the clothes but not take them away.","zh":"游客可以拍摄衣物，但不能带走。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Taking photos of museum objects can support later study without removing the originals.","zh":"拍摄馆藏可以支持后续学习，而不必移走原件。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-8cca5473f416","term":"take a photo of","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":71,"zh":"给……拍照","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"第24题找到的是一条牛仔裤；拍照是获准记录的方式，不是馆藏老照片。 · take the jeans away 把牛仔裤带走 · take a photo of the display 拍下展示","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"They couldn’t let us take them away, of course, but they did let us take a photo of them.","zh":"当然，他们不能让我们把裤子带走，但确实允许我们拍照。","source":"original","number":17},{"en":"You may take a photo of the object, but you cannot take it away.","zh":"可以拍摄展品，但不能带走。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I took a photo of the jacket instead of buying it.","zh":"我拍了夹克的照片，没有买它。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Visitors were allowed to photograph the clothes but not take them away.","zh":"游客可以拍摄衣物，但不能带走。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Taking photos of museum objects can support later study without removing the originals.","zh":"拍摄馆藏可以支持后续学习，而不必移走原件。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-3447e569537f","term":"go back to","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":72,"zh":"可追溯至……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"go back to the sixties 追溯到六十年代 · since then 从那以后","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, for the wall hangings, we’ll use our own jeans and those of our friends and family. We’ve got some going back to the sixties.","zh":"墙上的展示品会使用我们自己以及亲友的牛仔裤，其中一些可以追溯到二十世纪六十年代。","source":"original","number":19},{"en":"Some of these designs go back to the sixties.","zh":"部分设计可追溯到二十世纪六十年代。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I started wearing jeans at school and have liked them since then.","zh":"我上学时开始穿牛仔裤，从那以后一直喜欢。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The collection goes back to the sixties and has expanded since then.","zh":"收藏可追溯到六十年代，此后不断扩大。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Styles that go back several decades can remain relevant today.","zh":"可追溯到几十年前的风格如今仍可能有价值。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-9d2545dad520","term":"the sixties","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":73,"zh":"本篇指二十世纪六十年代","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"本文指二十世纪六十年代，即1960s，不是六十年以来。 · go back to the sixties 追溯到六十年代 · since then 从那以后","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Well, for the wall hangings, we’ll use our own jeans and those of our friends and family. We’ve got some going back to the sixties.","zh":"墙上的展示品会使用我们自己以及亲友的牛仔裤，其中一些可以追溯到二十世纪六十年代。","source":"original","number":19},{"en":"Some of these designs go back to the sixties.","zh":"部分设计可追溯到二十世纪六十年代。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I started wearing jeans at school and have liked them since then.","zh":"我上学时开始穿牛仔裤，从那以后一直喜欢。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The collection goes back to the sixties and has expanded since then.","zh":"收藏可追溯到六十年代，此后不断扩大。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Styles that go back several decades can remain relevant today.","zh":"可追溯到几十年前的风格如今仍可能有价值。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-6328bc502c5f","term":"since then","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":74,"zh":"从那以后","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"go back to the sixties 追溯到六十年代 · since then 从那以后","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"There’s never been a time since then when they’ve been out of style.","zh":"从那以后，牛仔裤从来没有过时过。","source":"original","number":20},{"en":"Some of these designs go back to the sixties.","zh":"部分设计可追溯到二十世纪六十年代。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I started wearing jeans at school and have liked them since then.","zh":"我上学时开始穿牛仔裤，从那以后一直喜欢。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The collection goes back to the sixties and has expanded since then.","zh":"收藏可追溯到六十年代，此后不断扩大。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Styles that go back several decades can remain relevant today.","zh":"可追溯到几十年前的风格如今仍可能有价值。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-eac3a306f533","term":"be out of style","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":75,"zh":"过时、不再流行","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"go out of style 过时 · remain in fashion 持续流行","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"There’s never been a time since then when they’ve been out of style.","zh":"从那以后，牛仔裤从来没有过时过。","source":"original","number":20},{"en":"This simple design has never been out of style.","zh":"这种简洁设计从未过时。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I don’t mind wearing clothes that are out of style.","zh":"我不介意穿过时的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article argues that classic jeans have never been out of style.","zh":"文章认为经典牛仔裤从未过时。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Products that do not go out of style may encourage longer use.","zh":"不过时的产品可能鼓励更长时间的使用。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-dbff213f1df6","term":"never been out of style","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":76,"zh":"从未过时","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"never＋out of style → 从未过时。 · go out of style 过时 · remain in fashion 持续流行","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"There’s never been a time since then when they’ve been out of style.","zh":"从那以后，牛仔裤从来没有过时过。","source":"original","number":20},{"en":"This simple design has never been out of style.","zh":"这种简洁设计从未过时。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I don’t mind wearing clothes that are out of style.","zh":"我不介意穿过时的衣服。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article argues that classic jeans have never been out of style.","zh":"文章认为经典牛仔裤从未过时。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Products that do not go out of style may encourage longer use.","zh":"不过时的产品可能鼓励更长时间的使用。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-1204540e5e31","term":"these days","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":77,"zh":"如今、现在","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"these days 如今 · the main attraction is not price 主要吸引力不是价格","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"That’s really the thing about jeans. And although they’re so durable, that’s not what people think about these days.","zh":"这才是牛仔裤的关键魅力。虽然它们很耐用，但这并不是如今人们主要考虑的事。","source":"original","number":21},{"en":"The main attraction is certainly not price, as the clothes are expensive.","zh":"主要吸引力肯定不是价格，因为衣服很贵。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"These days, I care more about comfort than price.","zh":"如今我更关注舒适而非价格。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The survey suggests that design, certainly not price, attracts most buyers.","zh":"调查表明吸引多数买家的是设计，肯定不是价格。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"These days, consumers may consider durability as well as price.","zh":"如今消费者可能同时考虑耐用性与价格。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-edba9cf2bcd6","term":"certainly not price","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":78,"zh":"肯定不是价格","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"these days 如今 · the main attraction is not price 主要吸引力不是价格","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And the main attraction’s certainly not price because they can be extremely expensive.","zh":"而且主要吸引力肯定不是价格，因为牛仔裤可能非常昂贵。","source":"original","number":22},{"en":"The main attraction is certainly not price, as the clothes are expensive.","zh":"主要吸引力肯定不是价格，因为衣服很贵。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"These days, I care more about comfort than price.","zh":"如今我更关注舒适而非价格。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The survey suggests that design, certainly not price, attracts most buyers.","zh":"调查表明吸引多数买家的是设计，肯定不是价格。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"These days, consumers may consider durability as well as price.","zh":"如今消费者可能同时考虑耐用性与价格。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-6c4f58fdf2e2","term":"although…that’s not what…","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":79,"zh":"虽然……但那并不是……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"although it is durable 虽然它耐用 · that is not what matters 那不是重要的事","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"That’s really the thing about jeans. And although they’re so durable, that’s not what people think about these days.","zh":"这才是牛仔裤的关键魅力。虽然它们很耐用，但这并不是如今人们主要考虑的事。","source":"original","number":21},{"en":"Although the coat is durable, that’s not what attracts buyers.","zh":"虽然外套耐用，但那不是吸引买家的原因。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Although it’s cheap, that’s not what I like most about it.","zh":"虽然它便宜，但这不是我最喜欢它的一点。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Although the product is popular, that is not what the report examines.","zh":"虽然产品流行，但报告研究的不是这一点。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Although economic growth is important, that is not what determines every aspect of well-being.","zh":"虽然经济增长重要，但它并不决定福祉的每个方面。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-6184985f7d04","term":"think of doing something","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":80,"zh":"考虑做某事","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"think of interviewing students 考虑采访学生 · consider using advertisements 考虑使用广告","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And for that, we’d thought of interviewing the other students about their opinions, but that wouldn’t be very visually interesting.","zh":"我们曾考虑采访其他学生，听听他们的意见，但这种形式在视觉上不太有吸引力。","source":"original","number":24},{"en":"We considered using interviews but chose advertisements instead.","zh":"我们考虑过访谈，但最后选择广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m thinking of taking a design course.","zh":"我正考虑上一门设计课程。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The team considered changing the display after receiving feedback.","zh":"团队收到反馈后考虑调整展示。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Schools should consider using visual materials to explain complex ideas.","zh":"学校应考虑用视觉材料解释复杂观点。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-34d17f65f755","term":"consider doing something","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":81,"zh":"考虑做某事","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"think of interviewing students 考虑采访学生 · consider using advertisements 考虑使用广告","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And for that, we’d thought of interviewing the other students about their opinions, but that wouldn’t be very visually interesting.","zh":"我们曾考虑采访其他学生，听听他们的意见，但这种形式在视觉上不太有吸引力。","source":"original","number":24},{"en":"We considered using interviews but chose advertisements instead.","zh":"我们考虑过访谈，但最后选择广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m thinking of taking a design course.","zh":"我正考虑上一门设计课程。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The team considered changing the display after receiving feedback.","zh":"团队收到反馈后考虑调整展示。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Schools should consider using visual materials to explain complex ideas.","zh":"学校应考虑用视觉材料解释复杂观点。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-49d674261480","term":"cut out…from…","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":82,"zh":"从……中剪下……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"cut ads out of magazines 从杂志剪广告 · look for quotes online 在网上找引语","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"So then we considered cutting out ads for designer jeans from magazines, and we found some really good ones.","zh":"于是我们考虑从杂志上剪下设计师品牌牛仔裤的广告，也找到了一些很不错的。","source":"original","number":25},{"en":"Please cut out two advertisements from the magazines.","zh":"请从杂志剪下两则广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I looked for information on the Internet before visiting.","zh":"参观前我在网上找信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The students cut pictures out of magazines and searched for background information online.","zh":"学生从杂志剪图片，并上网查背景信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Looking for information on the Internet requires careful evaluation of sources.","zh":"在网上寻找信息需要仔细评估来源。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-59a90253316f","term":"look for…on the Internet","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":83,"zh":"在网上寻找……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"cut ads out of magazines 从杂志剪广告 · look for quotes online 在网上找引语","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"So then we considered cutting out ads for designer jeans from magazines, and we found some really good ones.","zh":"于是我们考虑从杂志上剪下设计师品牌牛仔裤的广告，也找到了一些很不错的。","source":"original","number":25},{"en":"Please cut out two advertisements from the magazines.","zh":"请从杂志剪下两则广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I looked for information on the Internet before visiting.","zh":"参观前我在网上找信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The students cut pictures out of magazines and searched for background information online.","zh":"学生从杂志剪图片，并上网查背景信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Looking for information on the Internet requires careful evaluation of sources.","zh":"在网上寻找信息需要仔细评估来源。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-df864c0596aa","term":"abandon","type":"word","sourceOrder":84,"zh":"放弃","pos":"v.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"abandon an idea 放弃想法 · visually interesting displays 有视觉吸引力的展示","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"We’d thought of looking on the Internet for quotes from celebrities about their favorite designer labels, and we found some, but they didn’t really say much, so we abandoned that.","zh":"我们也想过上网找名人谈最喜爱设计师品牌的引语，确实找到了，但内容没什么实质信息，所以放弃了。","source":"original","number":26},{"en":"We abandoned the quotes because they didn’t really say much.","zh":"我们放弃引语，因为内容没有多少实质信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I abandoned my first idea because it wasn’t visually interesting.","zh":"我放弃最初想法，因为视觉上不吸引人。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The team abandoned an interview that did not provide useful information.","zh":"团队放弃了一段没有提供有用信息的访谈。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Students should abandon weak material when it does not support their main argument.","zh":"材料无法支持主要论点时，学生应放弃薄弱材料。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-b47e1a33df58","term":"wouldn’t be very visually interesting","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":85,"zh":"视觉上不会很有吸引力","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"abandon an idea 放弃想法 · visually interesting displays 有视觉吸引力的展示","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And for that, we’d thought of interviewing the other students about their opinions, but that wouldn’t be very visually interesting.","zh":"我们曾考虑采访其他学生，听听他们的意见，但这种形式在视觉上不太有吸引力。","source":"original","number":24},{"en":"We abandoned the quotes because they didn’t really say much.","zh":"我们放弃引语，因为内容没有多少实质信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I abandoned my first idea because it wasn’t visually interesting.","zh":"我放弃最初想法，因为视觉上不吸引人。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The team abandoned an interview that did not provide useful information.","zh":"团队放弃了一段没有提供有用信息的访谈。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Students should abandon weak material when it does not support their main argument.","zh":"材料无法支持主要论点时，学生应放弃薄弱材料。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d8d6dca52672","term":"didn’t really say much","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":86,"zh":"没有多少实质信息","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"abandon an idea 放弃想法 · visually interesting displays 有视觉吸引力的展示","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"We’d thought of looking on the Internet for quotes from celebrities about their favorite designer labels, and we found some, but they didn’t really say much, so we abandoned that.","zh":"我们也想过上网找名人谈最喜爱设计师品牌的引语，确实找到了，但内容没什么实质信息，所以放弃了。","source":"original","number":26},{"en":"We abandoned the quotes because they didn’t really say much.","zh":"我们放弃引语，因为内容没有多少实质信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I abandoned my first idea because it wasn’t visually interesting.","zh":"我放弃最初想法，因为视觉上不吸引人。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The team abandoned an interview that did not provide useful information.","zh":"团队放弃了一段没有提供有用信息的访谈。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Students should abandon weak material when it does not support their main argument.","zh":"材料无法支持主要论点时，学生应放弃薄弱材料。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-6bd1af689f0b","term":"more than adequately","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":87,"zh":"相当充分地、十分充分地","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"正面评价，意为相当充分；不能理解成例子太多应该删除。 · explain something adequately 充分解释某事 · and rightly so 而且这样做是对的","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Your section on history is very interesting, and I think you’ve illustrated your points more than adequately with relevant examples.","zh":"你们的历史部分很有趣，而且我认为你们已用相关例子相当充分地说明了观点。","source":"original","number":28},{"en":"You have explained the process more than adequately.","zh":"你已相当充分地解释过程。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The teacher praised our work, and rightly so.","zh":"老师表扬了我们的作业，而且确实该表扬。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report focuses on the evidence, and rightly so.","zh":"报告重视证据，而且理应如此。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Public services receive considerable attention, and rightly so, because they affect daily life.","zh":"公共服务受到广泛关注，而且理应如此，因为它们影响日常生活。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-2e45ceadc638","term":"and rightly so","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":88,"zh":"而且理应如此","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"肯定以历史为重点是合理的；后面要求补未来预测，并非删掉历史。 · explain something adequately 充分解释某事 · and rightly so 而且这样做是对的","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But though your emphasis is on the past, and rightly so, I’d like you to use your knowledge of the past to say where you think the whole thing might go.","zh":"不过，虽然你们以过去为重点，而且这样做是对的，我希望你们利用历史知识，谈谈牛仔裤今后可能如何发展。","source":"original","number":29},{"en":"You have explained the process more than adequately.","zh":"你已相当充分地解释过程。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The teacher praised our work, and rightly so.","zh":"老师表扬了我们的作业，而且确实该表扬。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report focuses on the evidence, and rightly so.","zh":"报告重视证据，而且理应如此。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Public services receive considerable attention, and rightly so, because they affect daily life.","zh":"公共服务受到广泛关注，而且理应如此，因为它们影响日常生活。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-37ff46a4ca66","term":"use knowledge of the past","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":89,"zh":"运用对过去的了解","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"use historical knowledge 运用历史知识 · predict future trends 预测未来趋势","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But though your emphasis is on the past, and rightly so, I’d like you to use your knowledge of the past to say where you think the whole thing might go.","zh":"不过，虽然你们以过去为重点，而且这样做是对的，我希望你们利用历史知识，谈谈牛仔裤今后可能如何发展。","source":"original","number":29},{"en":"Use your knowledge of the past to predict demand in ten years’ time.","zh":"利用历史知识预测十年后的需求。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I wonder where I’ll be in ten years’ time.","zh":"我好奇十年后自己会在哪里。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The study uses knowledge of the past to explore possible future trends.","zh":"研究利用历史知识探讨可能的未来趋势。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Policymakers can use knowledge of past changes when planning for the next decade.","zh":"政策制定者规划未来十年时可以利用对过去变化的了解。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-0d7c4aaaa831","term":"in ten years’ time","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":90,"zh":"十年后","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":4,"note":"use historical knowledge 运用历史知识 · predict future trends 预测未来趋势","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Will jeans still be bestsellers, say, in ten years’ time?","zh":"比如，十年后牛仔裤还会是畅销品吗？","source":"original","number":30},{"en":"Use your knowledge of the past to predict demand in ten years’ time.","zh":"利用历史知识预测十年后的需求。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I wonder where I’ll be in ten years’ time.","zh":"我好奇十年后自己会在哪里。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The study uses knowledge of the past to explore possible future trends.","zh":"研究利用历史知识探讨可能的未来趋势。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Policymakers can use knowledge of past changes when planning for the next decade.","zh":"政策制定者规划未来十年时可以利用对过去变化的了解。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-cc172d88aa16","term":"come up with","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":91,"zh":"想出、提出","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"come up with an idea 想出主意 · come up with a solution 提出解决方案","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Okay, we’ll see what we can come up with. Now, the next section we called Variety. We’ve got a lot about different brands and styles of jeans.","zh":"好的，我们看看能提出些什么。下一部分叫“多样性”，已写了很多不同品牌和款式的内容。","source":"original","number":31},{"en":"Can you come up with a prediction for the final section?","zh":"你能为最后一部分提出一项预测吗？","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"We came up with a better way to display the photos.","zh":"我们想出了更好的照片展示方式。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The team came up with a plan to reduce waste.","zh":"团队提出了减少浪费的计划。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Collaboration can help students come up with more effective solutions.","zh":"合作可以帮助学生提出更有效的解决方案。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-42fceed4a6d9","term":"add something about","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":92,"zh":"补充关于……的内容","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"add a section about practical uses 增加实际用途章节 · use jeans for work 穿牛仔裤工作","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But I think we need to add something about using jeans for work because they’re so comfortable and tough.","zh":"但我认为应补充牛仔裤用于工作的内容，因为它们舒适又耐穿。","source":"original","number":32},{"en":"Add something about how people use these clothes for work.","zh":"补充人们如何穿这些衣物工作的内容。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I use my old jeans for work around the house.","zh":"我穿旧牛仔裤做家务。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report adds information about clothes used for outdoor work.","zh":"报告补充户外工作服的信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Designers should consider how people use clothing for work.","zh":"设计师应考虑人们如何在工作中使用衣物。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-7fbe826ab300","term":"use something for work","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":93,"zh":"把某物用于工作","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"add a section about practical uses 增加实际用途章节 · use jeans for work 穿牛仔裤工作","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But I think we need to add something about using jeans for work because they’re so comfortable and tough.","zh":"但我认为应补充牛仔裤用于工作的内容，因为它们舒适又耐穿。","source":"original","number":32},{"en":"Add something about how people use these clothes for work.","zh":"补充人们如何穿这些衣物工作的内容。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I use my old jeans for work around the house.","zh":"我穿旧牛仔裤做家务。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report adds information about clothes used for outdoor work.","zh":"报告补充户外工作服的信息。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Designers should consider how people use clothing for work.","zh":"设计师应考虑人们如何在工作中使用衣物。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-9a7eb6ff1f5c","term":"not…by a long shot","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":94,"zh":"远远不是……，强烈否定","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"not just for style 远不只是为了时尚 · not finished by a long shot 离完成还远","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"They’re not just for style by a long shot. For example, even my dad wears them around the house all the time.","zh":"牛仔裤远远不只是为了时尚。例如，我爸爸也总是在家穿。","source":"original","number":33},{"en":"The project is not finished by a long shot.","zh":"项目离完成还远着呢。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"It’s not my favourite design by a long shot.","zh":"这远远算不上我最喜欢的设计。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The results were not conclusive by a long shot.","zh":"结果远远谈不上有定论。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Technology alone is not a complete solution by a long shot.","zh":"单靠技术远远不能算完整解决方案。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-1b5b07b2db3c","term":"go with the text","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":95,"zh":"与文字配合","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"drawings to go with the text 配合文字的图解 · be not bad at drawing 挺擅长画图","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I think it would be much easier if we had some step-by-step drawings to go with the text.","zh":"我觉得如果有配合文字的分步图解，就会容易理解得多。","source":"original","number":36},{"en":"We need some drawings to go with the text.","zh":"我们需要一些配合文字的图解。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m not bad at drawing simple diagrams.","zh":"我挺擅长画简单图表。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The illustrator produced diagrams to go with the text.","zh":"插画师制作配合文字的图表。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Illustrations that go with the text can improve readers’ understanding.","zh":"配合文字的插图可以改善读者理解。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-ddd403df9694","term":"be not bad at","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":96,"zh":"挺擅长……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"drawings to go with the text 配合文字的图解 · be not bad at drawing 挺擅长画图","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I think it would be much easier if we had some step-by-step drawings to go with the text.","zh":"我觉得如果有配合文字的分步图解，就会容易理解得多。","source":"original","number":36},{"en":"We need some drawings to go with the text.","zh":"我们需要一些配合文字的图解。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m not bad at drawing simple diagrams.","zh":"我挺擅长画简单图表。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The illustrator produced diagrams to go with the text.","zh":"插画师制作配合文字的图表。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Illustrations that go with the text can improve readers’ understanding.","zh":"配合文字的插图可以改善读者理解。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-a25f39107993","term":"could have been more clearly expressed","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":97,"zh":"原本可以表达得更清楚","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"technical information 技术信息 · express ideas clearly 清楚表达观点","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I thought that was quite good, but I must admit, I thought some of the technical stuff about making the cloth could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"我觉得那部分不错，但必须承认，有些布料制作的技术内容原本可以表达得更清楚。","source":"original","number":35},{"en":"Some technical details could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"一些技术细节原本可以表达得更清楚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"My explanation could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"我的解释原本可以更清楚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The reviewer felt that the technical section could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"评审认为技术章节原本可以表达得更清楚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Technical information should be clearly expressed for non-specialist readers.","zh":"技术信息应向非专业读者清楚表达。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-83e3b78f14e0","term":"technical","type":"word","sourceOrder":98,"zh":"技术性的","pos":"adj.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"technical information 技术信息 · express ideas clearly 清楚表达观点","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"I thought that was quite good, but I must admit, I thought some of the technical stuff about making the cloth could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"我觉得那部分不错，但必须承认，有些布料制作的技术内容原本可以表达得更清楚。","source":"original","number":35},{"en":"Some technical details could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"一些技术细节原本可以表达得更清楚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"My explanation could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"我的解释原本可以更清楚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The reviewer felt that the technical section could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"评审认为技术章节原本可以表达得更清楚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Technical information should be clearly expressed for non-specialist readers.","zh":"技术信息应向非专业读者清楚表达。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-a7f64bfc605e","term":"deal with","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":99,"zh":"涉及、讨论……","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"deal with advertising 讨论广告 · focus almost exclusively on… 几乎只关注……","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But you seem to deal almost exclusively with advertising in America and Europe.","zh":"但你们似乎几乎只讨论美国和欧洲的广告。","source":"original","number":39},{"en":"Your report deals almost exclusively with European advertising.","zh":"你的报告几乎只讨论欧洲广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"My project deals with the history of local clothing.","zh":"我的项目讨论当地服装历史。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article deals almost exclusively with online sales.","zh":"文章几乎只讨论线上销售。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Reports should not deal exclusively with wealthy countries when discussing global trends.","zh":"讨论全球趋势时，报告不应只涉及富裕国家。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-156f9a5147a0","term":"almost exclusively","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":100,"zh":"几乎只、几乎仅仅","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"deal with advertising 讨论广告 · focus almost exclusively on… 几乎只关注……","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But you seem to deal almost exclusively with advertising in America and Europe.","zh":"但你们似乎几乎只讨论美国和欧洲的广告。","source":"original","number":39},{"en":"Your report deals almost exclusively with European advertising.","zh":"你的报告几乎只讨论欧洲广告。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"My project deals with the history of local clothing.","zh":"我的项目讨论当地服装历史。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article deals almost exclusively with online sales.","zh":"文章几乎只讨论线上销售。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Reports should not deal exclusively with wealthy countries when discussing global trends.","zh":"讨论全球趋势时，报告不应只涉及富裕国家。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d82a8c54c981","term":"all corners of the earth","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":101,"zh":"世界各地、全球各个角落","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"对应全球视角，不是环保议题。 · reflect global trends 反映全球趋势 · argue that something matters 主张某事重要","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And in fact, marketing jeans is a huge phenomenon covering all corners of the earth. And your report should reflect that, shouldn’t it?","zh":"实际上，牛仔裤营销是遍及全球的现象，你们的报告也应体现这一点，对吧？","source":"original","number":40},{"en":"The report should reflect demand from all corners of the earth.","zh":"报告应反映世界各地的需求。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I enjoy meeting people from all corners of the earth.","zh":"我喜欢结识来自世界各地的人。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article argues that fashion reflects social changes around the world.","zh":"文章主张时尚反映全球社会变化。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Research should reflect different perspectives when making claims about global behaviour.","zh":"研究对全球行为作出判断时应体现不同视角。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-909ca0096d51","term":"reflect","type":"word","sourceOrder":102,"zh":"体现、反映","pos":"v.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"reflect global trends 反映全球趋势 · argue that something matters 主张某事重要","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And in fact, marketing jeans is a huge phenomenon covering all corners of the earth. And your report should reflect that, shouldn’t it?","zh":"实际上，牛仔裤营销是遍及全球的现象，你们的报告也应体现这一点，对吧？","source":"original","number":40},{"en":"The report should reflect demand from all corners of the earth.","zh":"报告应反映世界各地的需求。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I enjoy meeting people from all corners of the earth.","zh":"我喜欢结识来自世界各地的人。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article argues that fashion reflects social changes around the world.","zh":"文章主张时尚反映全球社会变化。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Research should reflect different perspectives when making claims about global behaviour.","zh":"研究对全球行为作出判断时应体现不同视角。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-d45a4e73e600","term":"argue that","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":103,"zh":"论证、主张……","pos":"v. + clause","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"reflect global trends 反映全球趋势 · argue that something matters 主张某事重要","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And in fact, marketing jeans is a huge phenomenon covering all corners of the earth. And your report should reflect that, shouldn’t it?","zh":"实际上，牛仔裤营销是遍及全球的现象，你们的报告也应体现这一点，对吧？","source":"original","number":40},{"en":"The report should reflect demand from all corners of the earth.","zh":"报告应反映世界各地的需求。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I enjoy meeting people from all corners of the earth.","zh":"我喜欢结识来自世界各地的人。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The article argues that fashion reflects social changes around the world.","zh":"文章主张时尚反映全球社会变化。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Research should reflect different perspectives when making claims about global behaviour.","zh":"研究对全球行为作出判断时应体现不同视角。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-c1928bf486e8","term":"a couple of","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":104,"zh":"几个、两三个，口语可泛指少数","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"a couple of articles 几篇文章 · a couple of useful examples 几个有用例子","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"You’re right. Actually, I found a couple of useful Internet articles that argue just that, so we can use those.","zh":"你说得对。我找到几篇有用的网络文章，正好论述这一点，可以用上。","source":"original","number":41},{"en":"I found a couple of useful articles for your project.","zh":"我找到几篇对你的项目有用的文章。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I bought a couple of books last week.","zh":"我上周买了几本书。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report includes a couple of examples from small businesses.","zh":"报告包含几个小企业的例子。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"A couple of well-chosen examples can make an argument more concrete.","zh":"几个精心选择的例子可以让论证更具体。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-ac6eb9b28a8c","term":"nowadays","type":"word","sourceOrder":105,"zh":"如今","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"nowadays, many people… 如今许多人…… · at first, people… 最初人们……","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But nowadays, most people associate jeans with rural America, the sorts of thing that farmers and workmen wore in the nineteenth century and afterwards.","zh":"不过如今，多数人把牛仔裤与美国乡村联系起来，也就是十九世纪及以后农民和工人穿着的那类衣物。","source":"original","number":7},{"en":"At first the design was practical; nowadays it is fashionable.","zh":"设计最初注重实用，如今则很时尚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"At first I disliked the course, but nowadays I enjoy it.","zh":"最初我不喜欢这门课，如今很享受。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"At first the shop sold workwear; nowadays it sells designer clothing.","zh":"商店最初出售工作服，如今出售设计师服装。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Nowadays, products often serve purposes different from those intended at first.","zh":"如今产品的用途常与最初设想不同。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-1589e7b7b027","term":"at first","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":106,"zh":"最初","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"nowadays, many people… 如今许多人…… · at first, people… 最初人们……","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","source":"original","number":13},{"en":"At first the design was practical; nowadays it is fashionable.","zh":"设计最初注重实用，如今则很时尚。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"At first I disliked the course, but nowadays I enjoy it.","zh":"最初我不喜欢这门课，如今很享受。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"At first the shop sold workwear; nowadays it sells designer clothing.","zh":"商店最初出售工作服，如今出售设计师服装。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Nowadays, products often serve purposes different from those intended at first.","zh":"如今产品的用途常与最初设想不同。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-7a7a40a4bb7b","term":"in the sixteenth century","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":107,"zh":"在十六世纪","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the sixteenth century 十六世纪 · the eighteen-forties 十九世纪四十年代","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But it’s actually from the Italian city of Genoa, where they made a similar fabric in the sixteenth century that was used for trousers worn by sailors.","zh":"但按材料所说，这个名称实际来自意大利城市 Genoa；当地十六世纪制作一种类似布料，用来做水手穿的裤子。","source":"original","number":6},{"en":"This object dates from the sixteenth century.","zh":"这件物品可追溯到十六世纪。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I saw a painting from the exact same year as the building.","zh":"我看过一幅与建筑完全同年的画。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The collection includes clothing from the eighteen-forties.","zh":"收藏包含十九世纪四十年代的衣物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Objects from the same year can reveal differences between social groups.","zh":"同一年的物品可以揭示社会群体之间的差异。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-5dd4bc5a6a44","term":"in the eighteen-forties","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":108,"zh":"在十九世纪四十年代，即 1840s","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the sixteenth century 十六世纪 · the eighteen-forties 十九世纪四十年代","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","source":"original","number":8},{"en":"This object dates from the sixteenth century.","zh":"这件物品可追溯到十六世纪。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I saw a painting from the exact same year as the building.","zh":"我看过一幅与建筑完全同年的画。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The collection includes clothing from the eighteen-forties.","zh":"收藏包含十九世纪四十年代的衣物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Objects from the same year can reveal differences between social groups.","zh":"同一年的物品可以揭示社会群体之间的差异。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-672623d2e6ee","term":"from that exact same year","type":"phrase","sourceOrder":109,"zh":"来自完全相同的那一年","pos":"语块","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the sixteenth century 十六世纪 · the eighteen-forties 十九世纪四十年代","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"And we were really lucky because they had a pair from that exact same year.","zh":"我们很幸运，因为他们正好有一条产自同一年的牛仔裤。","source":"original","number":16},{"en":"This object dates from the sixteenth century.","zh":"这件物品可追溯到十六世纪。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I saw a painting from the exact same year as the building.","zh":"我看过一幅与建筑完全同年的画。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The collection includes clothing from the eighteen-forties.","zh":"收藏包含十九世纪四十年代的衣物。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Objects from the same year can reveal differences between social groups.","zh":"同一年的物品可以揭示社会群体之间的差异。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-039d6add7ee0","term":"manufacturing","type":"word","sourceOrder":110,"zh":"制造、制造业","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the emphasis is on… 重点在于…… · manufacturing and marketing 制造与营销","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Now, you’ve also got a section called Manufacturing.","zh":"接着，你们还有一个名为“制造”的章节。","source":"original","number":34},{"en":"The emphasis in this section is on manufacturing.","zh":"这一章节重点讨论制造。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in both manufacturing and marketing.","zh":"我对制造和营销都感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report places more emphasis on marketing than on production.","zh":"报告对营销比对生产更加重视。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Companies need to consider both manufacturing costs and marketing strategies.","zh":"公司需要同时考虑制造成本与营销策略。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-e2a530e251d3","term":"marketing","type":"word","sourceOrder":111,"zh":"市场营销","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the emphasis is on… 重点在于…… · manufacturing and marketing 制造与营销","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"Your section on marketing seems good, especially the pictures you’ve included as examples.","zh":"营销部分看起来不错，尤其是你们用作例子的图片。","source":"original","number":38},{"en":"The emphasis in this section is on manufacturing.","zh":"这一章节重点讨论制造。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in both manufacturing and marketing.","zh":"我对制造和营销都感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report places more emphasis on marketing than on production.","zh":"报告对营销比对生产更加重视。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Companies need to consider both manufacturing costs and marketing strategies.","zh":"公司需要同时考虑制造成本与营销策略。","source":"supplemental"}]},{"id":"jeans-bd8c171b30dd","term":"emphasis","type":"word","sourceOrder":112,"zh":"重点、强调","pos":"n.","ipa":"","stars":3,"note":"the emphasis is on… 重点在于…… · manufacturing and marketing 制造与营销","paragraph":"听力原文","examples":[{"en":"But though your emphasis is on the past, and rightly so, I’d like you to use your knowledge of the past to say where you think the whole thing might go.","zh":"不过，虽然你们以过去为重点，而且这样做是对的，我希望你们利用历史知识，谈谈牛仔裤今后可能如何发展。","source":"original","number":29},{"en":"The emphasis in this section is on manufacturing.","zh":"这一章节重点讨论制造。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"I’m interested in both manufacturing and marketing.","zh":"我对制造和营销都感兴趣。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"The report places more emphasis on marketing than on production.","zh":"报告对营销比对生产更加重视。","source":"supplemental"},{"en":"Companies need to consider both manufacturing costs and marketing strategies.","zh":"公司需要同时考虑制造成本与营销策略。","source":"supplemental"}]}],"sentences":[{"en":"You will hear two fashion students called Tom and Sophie discussing their project on jeans with their lecturer.","zh":"你将听到两位时装专业学生 Tom 和 Sophie 与他们的讲师讨论牛仔裤项目。","paragraph":"已收录的原文摘句","speaker":"考官"},{"en":"Thanks for coming, Tom and Sophie. So you’re doing a project on jeans with a multimedia display and a written report.","zh":"谢谢你们来，Tom 和 Sophie。你们正在做牛仔裤项目，成果包括多媒体展示和书面报告。","paragraph":"项目任务与展示开场","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  Thanks for + doing；do a project on + 研究主题；with 引出配套成果。display 与 report 并列，后文分别讨论。\n听力抓手  先建立两个任务分区；前半段是 display，后半段才是 written report。"},{"en":"I’ve had a look at the plans for the display. Let’s start with that.","zh":"我看过展示方案了，我们先从这部分开始。","paragraph":"项目任务与展示开场","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  have a look at 看一看；plans for the display 是展示的方案；that 指展示方案。Let’s = let us，后接动词原形。\n听力抓手  start with that 标记讨论起点；此时不要把建议误归入书面报告。"},{"en":"So you’ve got a map to show where the name jeans comes from.","zh":"你们准备了一张地图，用来展示 jeans 这个名称的来源。","paragraph":"项目任务与展示开场","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  主干 you’ve got a map；to show 表目的；where the name jeans comes from 为 show 的宾语从句，用陈述语序。\n听力抓手  题目关心 word/name 的 origin，不是所有牛仔裤历史信息。"},{"en":"In fact, before we started the project, we both assumed it was somewhere in France because that’s where the jeans fabric, the denim, was first made.","zh":"实际上，做项目前，我们都以为这个名称源于法国某处，因为制作牛仔裤的布料 denim 最早产自那里。","paragraph":"原先误解与实际来源","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 we both assumed …；before 限定原先判断时间；because 解释误判理由；the denim 是 the jeans fabric 的同位说明；was first made 为被动结构。\n听力抓手  21 题答案跟 assumed 走。France 是过去想法，即使后面纠正了它，也仍回答 before 的问题。"},{"en":"But it’s actually from the Italian city of Genoa, where they made a similar fabric in the sixteenth century that was used for trousers worn by sailors.","zh":"但按材料所说，这个名称实际来自意大利城市 Genoa；当地十六世纪制作一种类似布料，用来做水手穿的裤子。","paragraph":"原先误解与实际来源","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 it’s actually from Genoa；where 补充当地的布料历史；that was used … 从句语义上修饰 a similar fabric；worn by sailors 是过去分词短语，修饰 trousers。\n听力抓手  But + actually 表示纠正旧观点，不表示 21 题改选实际来源。长句先抓名称来源，再处理布料用途。"},{"en":"But nowadays, most people associate jeans with rural America, the sorts of thing that farmers and workmen wore in the nineteenth century and afterwards.","zh":"不过如今，多数人把牛仔裤与美国乡村联系起来，也就是十九世纪及以后农民和工人穿着的那类衣物。","paragraph":"美国联想与电影选材","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  主干 people associate jeans with rural America；后部进一步说明服装联想。associate A with B 把 A 与 B 联系起来；that 引导定语从句，修饰 thing。\n听力抓手  nowadays 是第三种信息层级：现代联想。不要把它当作名称来源，也不要当作做项目前的想法。"},{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","paragraph":"美国联想与电影选材","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  两部分 you’re going to … 并列；show 后接 how 宾语从句；what made you decide 用 make + 宾语 + 动词原形。最后 that 指使用电影片段这个选择。\n听力抓手  老师先介绍板块，再追问素材选择理由。22 题要找随后的学生回答。"},{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","paragraph":"美国联想与电影选材","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 designs are accurate，且 it’ll give …；but 纠正“新电影不适合历史展示”的潜在担忧；where 从句修饰 setting。give someone a feel for 让某人感受或了解。\n听力抓手  recent 与 historical context 并不矛盾：拍摄时间新，服装与场景仍可以准确还原过去。"},{"en":"And anyway, nearly everyone enjoys cowboy movies.","zh":"而且，无论如何，几乎所有人都爱看牛仔电影。","paragraph":"美国联想与电影选材","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  anyway 补充附加理由；nearly 修饰 everyone，表示几乎所有人。\n听力抓手  娱乐性是附加说明；对应选项时优先使用上一句明确的历史场景作用。"},{"en":"Now, I’m glad you’ve included something about the pockets of the jeans because this was certainly something that attracted the original customers.","zh":"我很高兴你们写了牛仔裤口袋的内容，因为它确实吸引了最初的顾客。","paragraph":"口袋的装饰与实用性","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  主干 I’m glad …；because 说明评价原因；something that attracted … 中 that 从句修饰 something。original customers 指最初顾客，不是“原创顾客”。\n听力抓手  题干 originally 与 original customers 呼应，提醒回到早期购买原因。"},{"en":"Nowadays, manufacturers use all sorts of fancy stitches and designs on jeans pockets.","zh":"如今，制造商会在牛仔裤口袋上使用各种花哨缝线和图案。","paragraph":"口袋的装饰与实用性","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  主干 manufacturers use …；fancy 修饰 stitches and designs；on pockets 说明装饰位置。all sorts of = all kinds of。\n听力抓手  nowadays 是现代情况，23 题问早期，先记为非目标信息，等待 But。"},{"en":"But at first, people were more interested in the utilitarian side of things and the way the manufacturer used copper rivets, like little metal buttons, to make sure the pockets didn’t get torn off.","zh":"但最初，人们更关注实用性，特别是制造商用类似小金属扣的铜铆钉固定口袋，防止口袋被扯掉的做法。","paragraph":"口袋的装饰与实用性","speaker":"Tom","note":"结构与表达  主干 people were more interested in A and B；A = utilitarian side，B = the way …；to make sure 表目的；get torn off 为 get + 过去分词的被动表达。\n听力抓手  at first 对齐 originally；rivets → pockets didn’t get torn off → 固定结实 → 23 B。"},{"en":"They used them on both the jeans made from blue denim and those made of something called cotton duck, which was actually brown.","zh":"他们在蓝色 denim 制成的牛仔裤，以及棕色棉帆布 cotton duck 制成的牛仔裤上，都用了这种铆钉。","paragraph":"布料对比与博物馆藏品","speaker":"Tom","note":"结构与表达  They 按语境指制造者；them 指铜铆钉；both A and B 连接两类裤子；those 替代 jeans；made from / made of 为过去分词后置修饰。which 指 cotton duck。\n听力抓手  不同颜色随不同布料出现，不是对 23 题购买动机的解释。duck 在此是帆布，不是鸭子。"},{"en":"And we went to the museum because we wanted to see if they had something from eighteen seventy-three, because that was the year when Levi Strauss took out a patent on his design for jeans.","zh":"我们去博物馆，想看看有没有 1873 年的藏品，因为按材料所说，那一年 Levi Strauss 为他的牛仔裤设计取得了专利。","paragraph":"布料对比与博物馆藏品","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 we went to the museum；第一层 because 说明参观目的；see if 中 if 为“是否”，不是条件；第二层 because 解释为何关注 1873；when 修饰 year。\n听力抓手  design 属于选这个年份的理由，不说明找到的实物是设计稿。took out a patent 在此按取得专利理解，不宜直接译成“拿出专利”。"},{"en":"And we were really lucky because they had a pair from that exact same year.","zh":"我们很幸运，因为他们正好有一条产自同一年的牛仔裤。","paragraph":"布料对比与博物馆藏品","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 we were lucky；because 引导原因；a pair 后省略 of jeans；that exact same year 回指 1873。\n听力抓手  24 题核心直接在 had a pair；exact same 强化年份精确对应。"},{"en":"They couldn’t let us take them away, of course, but they did let us take a photo of them.","zh":"当然，他们不能让我们把裤子带走，但确实允许我们拍照。","paragraph":"布料对比与博物馆藏品","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  let + 宾语 + 动词原形；them 指牛仔裤；did 为助动词强调，之后仍用 let 原形。couldn’t … but did … 对比两种许可。\n听力抓手  找到的是裤子；获准进行的是拍照。不要把 take a photo 听成“博物馆里找到旧照片”。"},{"en":"Now, in your display, you’re planning to have a wall with thirty pairs of jeans hung on it. The wall’s titled The Attraction of Jeans. What exactly is their most significant attraction?","zh":"你们计划在展示中设置一面挂三十条牛仔裤的墙，题为“牛仔裤的魅力”。它们最主要的吸引力究竟是什么？","paragraph":"墙面展示与持续流行","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 planning to have a wall；with + 名词 + 过去分词：jeans hung on it；it 指 wall；their 指 jeans。significant 在这里表示重要的。\n听力抓手  题目问 most significant，与 main attraction 同义；不是问墙上有多少条裤子。"},{"en":"Well, for the wall hangings, we’ll use our own jeans and those of our friends and family. We’ve got some going back to the sixties.","zh":"墙上的展示品会使用我们自己以及亲友的牛仔裤，其中一些可以追溯到二十世纪六十年代。","paragraph":"墙面展示与持续流行","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  those 替代 jeans，避免重复；some 指一些牛仔裤；going back to … 作后置修饰，表示可追溯至某时期。\n听力抓手  the sixties 在本文历史语境下是 1960s，不是“已经六十年”。"},{"en":"There’s never been a time since then when they’ve been out of style.","zh":"从那以后，牛仔裤从来没有过时过。","paragraph":"墙面展示与持续流行","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 There has never been a time；since then 限定时间起点；when 从句修饰 time；never 否定“出现过过时的时期”。\n听力抓手  never + out of style → 一直流行 → 25 C。这是双层语义判断，不要只听出 style。"},{"en":"That’s really the thing about jeans. And although they’re so durable, that’s not what people think about these days.","zh":"这才是牛仔裤的关键魅力。虽然它们很耐用，但这并不是如今人们主要考虑的事。","paragraph":"排除耐用与价格","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  第一句 That 指前面持续流行这一特点；although 从句让步承认 durable；第二个 that 指耐用性；what people think about 作表语。\n听力抓手  同一个 that 可在相邻句中回指不同内容。although 后的耐用性真实，但 not what … 排除其作为如今主要关注点。"},{"en":"And the main attraction’s certainly not price because they can be extremely expensive.","zh":"而且主要吸引力肯定不是价格，因为牛仔裤可能非常昂贵。","paragraph":"排除耐用与价格","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  attraction’s = attraction is；certainly 强化否定；because 解释价格并不便宜；can 表可能。\n听力抓手  certainly not price → 排除 25 B。can be expensive 不意味着每条牛仔裤都昂贵，仍足以否定“价格合理是主要魅力”。"},{"en":"And then you’ve got a section in your display about designer labels.","zh":"接着，你们的展示里有一块关于设计师品牌的内容。","paragraph":"设计师品牌的素材筛选","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  section in the display 指展示板块；designer labels 在此为设计师品牌，而非仅指衣物上的纸质标签。\n听力抓手  切换到 26 题素材方案，不要还停留在 25 题吸引力。"},{"en":"And for that, we’d thought of interviewing the other students about their opinions, but that wouldn’t be very visually interesting.","zh":"我们曾考虑采访其他学生，听听他们的意见，但这种形式在视觉上不太有吸引力。","paragraph":"设计师品牌的素材筛选","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  we’d thought = we had thought；think of doing 考虑做；but 引出否定评价；第二个 that 指访谈方案。wouldn’t 描述预想效果。\n听力抓手  thought of 并非最终决定；but wouldn’t … 将访谈排除。"},{"en":"So then we considered cutting out ads for designer jeans from magazines, and we found some really good ones.","zh":"于是我们考虑从杂志上剪下设计师品牌牛仔裤的广告，也找到了一些很不错的。","paragraph":"设计师品牌的素材筛选","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  consider + doing；cut out 剪下；ones 替代 ads；really good 为正面评价。\n听力抓手  magazines + ads → magazine advertisements；方案得到支持，对应 26 C。"},{"en":"We’d thought of looking on the Internet for quotes from celebrities about their favorite designer labels, and we found some, but they didn’t really say much, so we abandoned that.","zh":"我们也想过上网找名人谈最喜爱设计师品牌的引语，确实找到了，但内容没什么实质信息，所以放弃了。","paragraph":"设计师品牌的素材筛选","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 thought of looking … and found some；but 给否定评价；so 引出 abandoned 的结果；they 指引语；that 指用名人引语的方案。\n听力抓手  方案被提及并且找到材料，不等于会采用。最后状态 abandoned → 排除 26 B。"},{"en":"Uh, now let’s look at possible improvements to the draft of your written report.","zh":"现在来看看书面报告草稿可以怎样改进。","paragraph":"书面报告与历史评价","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  look at 在此为审视、讨论；improvements to … 对……的改进；draft 指草稿。\n听力抓手  report 标记进入 27–30 匹配题；后面四个章节都在报告内，不是展示素材选择。"},{"en":"Your section on history is very interesting, and I think you’ve illustrated your points more than adequately with relevant examples.","zh":"你们的历史部分很有趣，而且我认为你们已用相关例子相当充分地说明了观点。","paragraph":"书面报告与历史评价","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  I think 后接宾语从句；illustrate your points 说明观点；with relevant examples 表示方法；more than adequately 为“非常充分地”，不是负面批评例子过多。\n听力抓手  这是肯定：interesting、relevant、adequately。27 题不能据此选删除无关信息 G。"},{"en":"But though your emphasis is on the past, and rightly so, I’d like you to use your knowledge of the past to say where you think the whole thing might go.","zh":"不过，虽然你们以过去为重点，而且这样做是对的，我希望你们利用历史知识，谈谈牛仔裤今后可能如何发展。","paragraph":"书面报告与历史评价","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 I’d like you to use …；though 引导让步；and rightly so 为插入评价；to say 表目的；where … might go 为间接问句，指发展方向而非地理目的地。\n听力抓手  But 后才是改进要求。保留历史重点，同时增加有历史依据的未来判断。"},{"en":"Will jeans still be bestsellers, say, in ten years’ time?","zh":"比如，十年后牛仔裤还会是畅销品吗？","paragraph":"未来预测与多样性章节","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  Will … still be … 为未来疑问；bestsellers 可指畅销商品，不限于畅销书；say 为插入语“比如”；in ten years’ time 指十年后。\n听力抓手  这句把抽象的 where … might go 具体化为未来销量预测，锁定 27 E。"},{"en":"Okay, we’ll see what we can come up with. Now, the next section we called Variety. We’ve got a lot about different brands and styles of jeans.","zh":"好的，我们看看能提出些什么。下一部分叫“多样性”，已写了很多不同品牌和款式的内容。","paragraph":"未来预测与多样性章节","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  come up with 提出或想出；what 引导 see 的宾语从句；the next section 前置为话题；brands and styles 为已有内容。\n听力抓手  学生接受补预测，随后 Now, the next section 切换到 28 题；品牌和款式是当前内容，不是新增建议。"},{"en":"But I think we need to add something about using jeans for work because they’re so comfortable and tough.","zh":"但我认为应补充牛仔裤用于工作的内容，因为它们舒适又耐穿。","paragraph":"未来预测与多样性章节","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 I think we need to add something；about using … 说明新增内容；because 引导原因；tough 描述布料结实耐磨。\n听力抓手  But + need to add → 修改动作。using … for work 对应 practical uses，不是更多款式。"},{"en":"They’re not just for style by a long shot. For example, even my dad wears them around the house all the time.","zh":"牛仔裤远远不只是为了时尚。例如，我爸爸也总是在家穿。","paragraph":"未来预测与多样性章节","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  not … by a long shot 加强否定；even 强调出乎预期的例子；wear them around the house 表示在家日常穿着，不必译成穿着到处走动。\n听力抓手  爸爸的例子说明日常实用用途，不是说只适合工作或只适合男性。"},{"en":"Now, you’ve also got a section called Manufacturing.","zh":"接着，你们还有一个名为“制造”的章节。","paragraph":"制造章节的问题与解决方法","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  called Manufacturing 是过去分词短语，修饰 section，相当于 which is called …。\n听力抓手  章节名出现，切换到 29 题；不要把后面的图解建议放到 Marketing。"},{"en":"I thought that was quite good, but I must admit, I thought some of the technical stuff about making the cloth could have been more clearly expressed.","zh":"我觉得那部分不错，但必须承认，有些布料制作的技术内容原本可以表达得更清楚。","paragraph":"制造章节的问题与解决方法","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 I thought … could have been …；could have been + 过去分词，对已经写出的草稿作委婉批评；about making the cloth 限定 technical stuff 内容。\n听力抓手  quite good 是总体肯定，but 后指出 clarity 问题。问题是解释不清，不是技术内容无关。"},{"en":"I think it would be much easier if we had some step-by-step drawings to go with the text.","zh":"我觉得如果有配合文字的分步图解，就会容易理解得多。","paragraph":"制造章节的问题与解决方法","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 it would be much easier；if we had 为设想条件；to go with the text 修饰 drawings，表示图文配合；much 修饰比较级 easier。\n听力抓手  drawings → visual illustrations → 29 C。比只听出 easier 更关键的是识别具体解决办法。"},{"en":"I’m not bad at that, so I’ll do that.","zh":"我挺擅长画这种图，所以由我来做。","paragraph":"制造章节的问题与解决方法","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  not bad at 为含蓄肯定“挺擅长”；前后 that 都指画分步图；so 连接能力与承担任务的结果。\n听力抓手  I’ll do that 确认方案落实，也表明画图由 Tom 承担。不要把 not bad 错听为“不擅长”。"},{"en":"Your section on marketing seems good, especially the pictures you’ve included as examples.","zh":"营销部分看起来不错，尤其是你们用作例子的图片。","paragraph":"营销范围与最终修改","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 section seems good；especially 强调优点；pictures 后省略 that 的定语从句；as examples 为作为例子。\n听力抓手  图片已被肯定，30 题的重点不是要求补图。"},{"en":"But you seem to deal almost exclusively with advertising in America and Europe.","zh":"但你们似乎几乎只讨论美国和欧洲的广告。","paragraph":"营销范围与最终修改","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  seem to do 表委婉判断；deal with 涉及、讨论；almost exclusively 几乎仅仅，限定了当前报告覆盖范围。\n听力抓手  But 后明确不足：范围太局限。America and Europe 是现有区域，不是未来要增加的区域。"},{"en":"And in fact, marketing jeans is a huge phenomenon covering all corners of the earth. And your report should reflect that, shouldn’t it?","zh":"实际上，牛仔裤营销是遍及全球的现象，你们的报告也应体现这一点，对吧？","paragraph":"营销范围与最终修改","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  marketing jeans 为动名词短语作主语；covering … 分词短语修饰 phenomenon；reflect that 指反映全球范围；shouldn’t it 为附加问句。\n听力抓手  all corners of the earth → global aspects → 30 B。earth 在此为全球范围，不是环保议题。"},{"en":"You’re right. Actually, I found a couple of useful Internet articles that argue just that, so we can use those.","zh":"你说得对。我找到几篇有用的网络文章，正好论述这一点，可以用上。","paragraph":"营销范围与最终修改","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  that argue … 为定语从句，修饰 articles；argue that 表提出或论证观点，不是争吵；just that 强调刚才所说的全球性；those 指文章。\n听力抓手  学生确认导师建议，并提出可使用的资料来源。找到 Internet articles 是执行方式，global aspects 才是新增内容。"}],"questions":[{"number":21,"question":"Before doing their project, the students thought the origin of the word ‘jeans’ was …","answer":"C","chosen":"A","focus":"答题链  Before → assumed → France → C。A 与后面的实际发现有关，即使它更接近材料所讲的真实来源，也不是“做项目前的想法”。原文区分 jeans 名称与 denim 布料，不要把两者合并。","mistake":"推测：忽略 Before，可能把后来查明的 Genoa 当成最初猜测。","method":"听到 assumed 时先记下最初想法，随后另记 But 后的最终发现。","evidence":[{"en":"In fact, before we started the project, we both assumed it was somewhere in France because that’s where the jeans fabric, the denim, was first made.","zh":"实际上，做项目前，我们都以为这个名称源于法国某处，因为制作牛仔裤的布料 denim 最早产自那里。","paragraph":"原先误解与实际来源","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 we both assumed …；before 限定原先判断时间；because 解释误判理由；the denim 是 the jeans fabric 的同位说明；was first made 为被动结构。\n听力抓手  21 题答案跟 assumed 走。France 是过去想法，即使后面纠正了它，也仍回答 before 的问题。","highlight":"somewhere in France"},{"en":"But it’s actually from the Italian city of Genoa, where they made a similar fabric in the sixteenth century that was used for trousers worn by sailors.","zh":"但按材料所说，这个名称实际来自意大利城市 Genoa；当地十六世纪制作一种类似布料，用来做水手穿的裤子。","paragraph":"原先误解与实际来源","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 it’s actually from Genoa；where 补充当地的布料历史；that was used … 从句语义上修饰 a similar fabric；worn by sailors 是过去分词短语，修饰 trousers。\n听力抓手  But + actually 表示纠正旧观点，不表示 21 题改选实际来源。长句先抓名称来源，再处理布料用途。","highlight":""},{"en":"But nowadays, most people associate jeans with rural America, the sorts of thing that farmers and workmen wore in the nineteenth century and afterwards.","zh":"不过如今，多数人把牛仔裤与美国乡村联系起来，也就是十九世纪及以后农民和工人穿着的那类衣物。","paragraph":"美国联想与电影选材","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  主干 people associate jeans with rural America；后部进一步说明服装联想。associate A with B 把 A 与 B 联系起来；that 引导定语从句，修饰 thing。\n听力抓手  nowadays 是第三种信息层级：现代联想。不要把它当作名称来源，也不要当作做项目前的想法。","highlight":""}],"wrong":true,"type":"单项选择","instruction":"","choices":["A a material created in an Italian city","B clothing worn in the American countryside","C a fabric made in France"]},{"number":22,"question":"Why did the students plan to use a cowboy film excerpt in their display?","answer":"A","chosen":"C","focus":"答题链  costume 准确 → 让观众感受当时的穿着场景 → historical context → A。导师先说这块展示要讲“如何越来越流行”，那是板块主题；学生解释使用影片的具体理由则是还原历史环境。C 混用了板块主题与素材用途。","mistake":"推测：排除 B  accurate for the period 是“符合那个年代”，并未说明设计被怎样改造。nearly everyone enjoys cowboy movies 只是附加的轻松理由，不取代明确的历史背景用途。","method":"分开记录展示主题和电影片段的用途，等学生解释 give our audience a feel for。","evidence":[{"en":"Then you’re going to show how jeans became increasingly popular in the eighteen-forties, and you’re going to use a short clip from a cowboy movie for that. So what made you decide to do that?","zh":"接着，你们要介绍牛仔裤在十九世纪四十年代如何越来越受欢迎，并使用牛仔电影短片段。你们为什么决定这样做？","paragraph":"美国联想与电影选材","speaker":"导师","note":"结构与表达  两部分 you’re going to … 并列；show 后接 how 宾语从句；what made you decide 用 make + 宾语 + 动词原形。最后 that 指使用电影片段这个选择。\n听力抓手  老师先介绍板块，再追问素材选择理由。22 题要找随后的学生回答。","highlight":""},{"en":"Well, the movie’s very recent, but in fact, the costume designs are accurate for the period, and it’ll give our audience a feel for the sort of setting where jeans were worn at that time in America.","zh":"电影虽是近期作品，但服装设计符合那个时代，能让观众感受当时美国人穿牛仔裤的场景。","paragraph":"美国联想与电影选材","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 designs are accurate，且 it’ll give …；but 纠正“新电影不适合历史展示”的潜在担忧；where 从句修饰 setting。give someone a feel for 让某人感受或了解。\n听力抓手  recent 与 historical context 并不矛盾：拍摄时间新，服装与场景仍可以准确还原过去。","highlight":"a feel for"}],"wrong":true,"type":"单项选择","instruction":"","choices":["A to provide a historical context for jeans","B to show how the design of jeans was adapted","C to illustrate why jeans originally became popular"]},{"number":24,"question":"What item from 1873 did the students find in a museum?","answer":"A","chosen":"B","focus":"数量与译法  a pair of jeans 是一条牛仔裤；不能因为 pair 是“一双、一对”就想象成两条。they had a pair 中省略 of jeans。原文并未直接出现 original pair，答案依据是“来自 1873 年的一条牛仔裤实物”。","mistake":"推测：可能将专利 design 当成出现在博物馆的实物，也可能被后面的 photo 带走。","method":"先找 they had 的宾语，再判断 take away 和 take a photo 分别指什么。","evidence":[{"en":"And we went to the museum because we wanted to see if they had something from eighteen seventy-three, because that was the year when Levi Strauss took out a patent on his design for jeans.","zh":"我们去博物馆，想看看有没有 1873 年的藏品，因为按材料所说，那一年 Levi Strauss 为他的牛仔裤设计取得了专利。","paragraph":"布料对比与博物馆藏品","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 we went to the museum；第一层 because 说明参观目的；see if 中 if 为“是否”，不是条件；第二层 because 解释为何关注 1873；when 修饰 year。\n听力抓手  design 属于选这个年份的理由，不说明找到的实物是设计稿。took out a patent 在此按取得专利理解，不宜直接译成“拿出专利”。","highlight":""},{"en":"And we were really lucky because they had a pair from that exact same year.","zh":"我们很幸运，因为他们正好有一条产自同一年的牛仔裤。","paragraph":"布料对比与博物馆藏品","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  主干 we were lucky；because 引导原因；a pair 后省略 of jeans；that exact same year 回指 1873。\n听力抓手  24 题核心直接在 had a pair；exact same 强化年份精确对应。","highlight":"a pair from that exact same year"},{"en":"They couldn’t let us take them away, of course, but they did let us take a photo of them.","zh":"当然，他们不能让我们把裤子带走，但确实允许我们拍照。","paragraph":"布料对比与博物馆藏品","speaker":"学生","note":"结构与表达  let + 宾语 + 动词原形；them 指牛仔裤；did 为助动词强调，之后仍用 let 原形。couldn’t … but did … 对比两种许可。\n听力抓手  找到的是裤子；获准进行的是拍照。不要把 take a photo 听成“博物馆里找到旧照片”。","highlight":""}],"wrong":true,"type":"单项选择","instruction":"","choices":["A an original pair of jeans","B an early design for a pair of jeans","C an old photograph of someone wearing jeans"]},{"number":25,"question":"What do the students think is the main attraction of jeans for most people?","answer":"C","chosen":"A","focus":"判断链  从二十世纪六十年代起未过时 → 持续时尚 → C。durable 的确是优点，但 although … not what … 明确排除其作为如今主要关注点；price 也被 certainly not 否定。","mistake":"推测：你的 A 可能来自只识别到 durable，未处理后半句的否定。复听时分两栏：特点是否存在／是否为主要吸引力。真实特点不自动等于正确答案。","method":"听到 although / not 时把该项划掉，再确认什么是 main attraction。","evidence":[{"en":"There’s never been a time since then when they’ve been out of style.","zh":"从那以后，牛仔裤从来没有过时过。","paragraph":"墙面展示与持续流行","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 There has never been a time；since then 限定时间起点；when 从句修饰 time；never 否定“出现过过时的时期”。\n听力抓手  never + out of style → 一直流行 → 25 C。这是双层语义判断，不要只听出 style。","highlight":"out of style"},{"en":"That’s really the thing about jeans. And although they’re so durable, that’s not what people think about these days.","zh":"这才是牛仔裤的关键魅力。虽然它们很耐用，但这并不是如今人们主要考虑的事。","paragraph":"排除耐用与价格","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  第一句 That 指前面持续流行这一特点；although 从句让步承认 durable；第二个 that 指耐用性；what people think about 作表语。\n听力抓手  同一个 that 可在相邻句中回指不同内容。although 后的耐用性真实，但 not what … 排除其作为如今主要关注点。","highlight":""},{"en":"And the main attraction’s certainly not price because they can be extremely expensive.","zh":"而且主要吸引力肯定不是价格，因为牛仔裤可能非常昂贵。","paragraph":"排除耐用与价格","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  attraction’s = attraction is；certainly 强化否定；because 解释价格并不便宜；can 表可能。\n听力抓手  certainly not price → 排除 25 B。can be expensive 不意味着每条牛仔裤都昂贵，仍足以否定“价格合理是主要魅力”。","highlight":""}],"wrong":true,"type":"单项选择","instruction":"","choices":["A they are long-lasting","B they are reasonably priced","C they are always in fashion"]},{"number":27,"question":"History","answer":"E","chosen":"G","focus":"逻辑链  历史部分有趣 → 例子相关且充分 → 以历史知识为依据讨论未来 → E。导师并未说内容不相关，relevant examples 反而直接削弱 G；more than adequately 是“相当充分”，不是“例子太多，应删除”。","mistake":"推测：though … and rightly so 表示承认以过去为重点是对的；But 引出下一步补充，不能理解为要删掉历史。say 在这里为“比如”，十年后只是示例时间，不是要学生复述当前销量。","method":"先听老师是否否定现有内容，再等 But 后提出的具体修改。","evidence":[{"en":"Your section on history is very interesting, and I think you’ve illustrated your points more than adequately with relevant examples.","zh":"你们的历史部分很有趣，而且我认为你们已用相关例子相当充分地说明了观点。","paragraph":"书面报告与历史评价","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  I think 后接宾语从句；illustrate your points 说明观点；with relevant examples 表示方法；more than adequately 为“非常充分地”，不是负面批评例子过多。\n听力抓手  这是肯定：interesting、relevant、adequately。27 题不能据此选删除无关信息 G。","highlight":""},{"en":"But though your emphasis is on the past, and rightly so, I’d like you to use your knowledge of the past to say where you think the whole thing might go.","zh":"不过，虽然你们以过去为重点，而且这样做是对的，我希望你们利用历史知识，谈谈牛仔裤今后可能如何发展。","paragraph":"书面报告与历史评价","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  主干 I’d like you to use …；though 引导让步；and rightly so 为插入评价；to say 表目的；where … might go 为间接问句，指发展方向而非地理目的地。\n听力抓手  But 后才是改进要求。保留历史重点，同时增加有历史依据的未来判断。","highlight":"where you think the whole thing might go"},{"en":"Will jeans still be bestsellers, say, in ten years’ time?","zh":"比如，十年后牛仔裤还会是畅销品吗？","paragraph":"未来预测与多样性章节","speaker":"","note":"结构与表达  Will … still be … 为未来疑问；bestsellers 可指畅销商品，不限于畅销书；say 为插入语“比如”；in ten years’ time 指十年后。\n听力抓手  这句把抽象的 where … might go 具体化为未来销量预测，锁定 27 E。","highlight":""}],"wrong":true,"type":"配对题","instruction":"","choices":["A Include more on practical uses of jeans","B Add information about global aspects","C Use visual illustrations","G Remove irrelevant information"],"questionNote":"现存原题截图可核对 A、B、C、G。E 的英文原措辞待补，题解记载的意思是预测未来走向。","optionsNotice":"现有题目资料只收录了上面这些选项。"}],"examples":[]};
